apa101.com/places/phra-narai/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/phra-narai/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Parks & Public Spaces</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place notes · Parks and public spaces</span><h1>Phra Narai Park</h1><p class="english">Phra Narai Park</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">5 verified items</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="phra-narai">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/phra-narai.webp" alt="สวนสาธารณะพระนารายณ์" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8696046, 98.3445279 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8696046,98.3445279" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd>076 421 750 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Contact information ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>The park's origins remain behind a veil of evidence</h3><p class="era-years"></p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>For Phra Narai Public Park itself, no document has been found stating its construction year, initiator, or reason for establishment. It should therefore not be concluded that the park originated in the tin-mining era or during the period of the town governors merely because Takuapa prospered then.</p><p>What can be confirmed is that the park is in front of Takuapa Town Municipality Office and houses a statue of Phra Narai with replicas of attendant deities. Phra Narai is significant to the town and is used in the municipal emblem, but this evidence explains the significance of the deity and the town, not the park's founding date.</p><p>Takua Pa's context in municipal documents reflects an old town shaped by trade, tin mining, Sino-Portuguese buildings, and a large Chinese community. However, no evidence directly links these elements to the park's construction.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) Environmental Operation Plan</a> · <a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sun Khomun Klang Watthanatham (Cultural Information Center)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>From a sacred space to a town activity stage</h3><p class="era-years">No verifiable timeline has been found.</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The evidence found does not record any transfer of ownership, abandonment, or restoration of the park over time, so it cannot yet be answered whether the park experienced these events. The same applies to the impact of the 2004 tsunami (B.E. 2547), for which no report specifically about this park has been found.</p><p>During the period covered by the available information, the park's role expanded from a place of worship to a public space for the town. It is used for cultural activities, recreation, traditional events, Children's Day events, and as a playground, under the management of Takuapa Town Municipality.</p><p>Old-town documents identify several places and ancient monuments in the municipality, but no Fine Arts Department announcement has been found registering “Phra Narai Park Public Garden” directly as an ancient monument. The park is therefore carefully distinguished from nearby ancient monuments.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sun Khomun Klang Watthanatham (Cultural Information Center)</a> · <a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takua Pa Old Town boundary delineation project</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A public park in the 2026 context</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The latest publicly available information confirms that the park remains a public space under the care of Takuapa Town Municipality. It contains statues of Phra Narai and attendant deities for worship, as well as a playground and community recreation areas.</p><p>The park also serves as the town's central stage. The Phra Narai worship ceremony and Takua Pa local-products event were held here in 2025 (B.E. 2568), with reports of Takua Pa local-products activities at the park's central stage. The 2023 (B.E. 2566) annual event ran from 27 March to 5 April.</p><p>No official information has been found confirming opening and closing hours, admission fees, the latest physical condition, or a completed construction project. For the proposed “Narai Hub &amp; Commercial Center”, only policy or guidance reports from municipal administrators have been found, so it is not yet considered a completed project.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sun Khomun Klang Watthanatham (Cultural Information Center)</a> · <a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/609307" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Siam Rath</a> · <a href="https://www.thaipr.net/travel/3321904" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ThaiPR.NET</a> · <a href="https://www.naewna.com/lady/892595" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Naewna</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">27 March to 5 April 2023 (B.E. 2566)</p><h3>Phra Narai worship ceremony</h3><p>The annual event is held at Phra Narai Public Park, along with cultural activities and community products.</p><a href="https://www.thaipr.net/travel/3321904" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2025 (2568 BE)</p><h3>Takua Pa good products fair</h3><p>The central stage of the community economic promotion project was held in the park.</p><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/609307" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2026 (2569 BE)</p><h3>Current status</h3><p>It remains a public park under the municipality's care. It features a worship point, a playground, and an event space.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>The year the park was built has not been found</h3><p>The disclosed documents do not specify the year, founder, or park establishment project.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Phra Narai statue as a city symbol</h3><p>The municipality document states that the Phra Narai statue is sacred to the townspeople and is used as the municipality seal, but does not specify the year it was enshrined in the park.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Phra Narai and attendant statues</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Replicas of the deities enshrined in the park. The originals are ancient sculptures from the Khao Phra Narai archaeological site, now in the Thalang National Museum.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Municipal symbol</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The Phra Narai image is used as the emblem of Takua Pa Town Municipality, reflecting the town's historical roots linked to Indian culture.</p><a href="https://www.phangngaedarea.go.th/site/wp-content/uploads/pdf/17225631.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Proximity to the Sunday Market</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The park is a landmark near the Takua Pa Old Town Sunday Market, often used as an activity space or gathering point for festivals.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Event area</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Used for municipal cultural activities, recreation, and local traditional events</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2025-03-14 · ThailandTravel</p><h3>Phra Narai Worship and Takua Pa Good Products Fair 2025 (2568 BE)</h3><p>Announced the event schedule for 14 to 23 March 2025 at the park.</p><a href="https://thailandtravel.app/content/read/3344" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2023-03-31 · ThaiPR.NET</p><h3>Phra Narai worship ceremony, an identity of Takua Pa people</h3><p>Reported on the annual event in 2023 (2566 BE), which was held at the park between 27 March and 5 April.</p><a href="https://www.thaipr.net/travel/3321904" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted"> · Siam Rath</p><h3>Takua Pa Town Municipality organised community economic promotion activities, Takua Pa good products</h3><p>Used the park's central stage as the area for the 2025 community economic promotion project.</p><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/609307" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The Phra Narai statues in the park are replicas; the original ancient sculptures were moved for safekeeping at the Thalang National Museum in Phuket.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The Phra Narai image is the official emblem of Takua Pa Town Municipality.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located on Si Takua Pa Road, in front of the Takua Pa Town Municipality office, in the old town area.</p><a href="https://www.phangngaedarea.go.th/site/wp-content/uploads/pdf/17225631.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li><a href="/en/places/thung-phra/">Thung Phra Pho Park</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Located on Si Takua Pa Road, in front of the Takua Pa Town Municipality office, in the old town area.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>The park is managed by Takuapa Town Municipality. It is a place for recreation and houses statues of Phra Narai and replicas of attendant deities.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>A Phra Narai devotional sculpture is available for public worship. According to official sources, the park contains Phra Narai and replicas of attendant deities, and part of the park is a playground.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Cultural Information Centre (m-culture)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AAาธารณะอุทยานพระนารายณ์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Phang Nga Primary Educational Service Area Office</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.phangngaedarea.go.th/site/wp-content/uploads/pdf/17225631.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ThaiPR.NET</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.thaipr.net/travel/3321904" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">MGR Online</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9550000099132" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sun Khomun Klang Watthanatham (Cultural Information Center)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) Environmental Operation Plan</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Siam Rath</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/609307" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Naewna</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.naewna.com/lady/892595" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Published and verified opening hours are not verified.</li><li>Admission fee data is not verified.</li><li>Current conditions of facilities like restrooms, parking, and wheelchair accessibility are not verified for 2026.</li><li>The specific schedule for the annual Phra Narai worship ceremony is not confirmed.</li><li>Verified distance from Phuket, Khao Lak, or the airport not found.</li><li>No information on the construction year or builder has been found.</li><li>No evidence confirming the park's role during the tin-mining era has been found.</li><li>No evidence was found confirming Sino-Portuguese or Chinese architecture at the garden</li><li>No evidence was found that the garden is registered as an ancient monument</li><li>No nearby places with a verified walking distance were found</li><li>No verified event month or lunar calendar information was found</li><li>The garden's construction year and builder</li><li>The garden's original purpose or founding project</li><li>The history of ownership changes, abandonment, or restoration</li><li>Evidence of impact from the 2004 tsunami ( พ.ศ. 2547 )</li><li>The year the garden itself was registered as an ancient monument</li><li>Opening and closing hours, admission fees, and the latest condition of buildings and structures</li><li>Whether the Narai Hub project is actually underway</li><li>No old image explicitly identified as showing the garden has been found</li><li>No direct URL for a current image file with verifiable usage rights has been found</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
site\en\places\kue-chai\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Kue Chai Tung Shrine · Kue Chai Tueng Shrine · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="Telling the culture of worship through the shrine&#x27;s details · Takuapa Chinese shrine · Takuapa Old Town shrine · Phang Nga shrine"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Kue Chai Tung Shrine · Kue Chai Tueng Shrine"><meta property="og:description" content="Telling the culture of worship through the shrine&#x27;s details · Takuapa Chinese shrine · Takuapa Old Town shrine · Phang Nga shrine"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/places/kue-chai/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/kue-chai.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/kue-chai.png"><meta name="generator" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/kue-chai/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "หน้าแรก", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "ศาลเจ้ากู่ใช่ตึ๋ง · ศาลเจ้าพ่อกวนอู", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/places/kue-chai/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "TouristAttraction", "name": "ศาลเจ้ากู่ใช่ตึ๋ง", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/kue-chai/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/kue-chai.webp", "description": "เอกสารกล่าวถึงการขอพรด้านสุขภาพและโชคลาภ", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "บ้านเลขที่ 87 ถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.8265089587, "longitude": 98.3647240165}}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "ควรแต่งกายอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "แต่งกายสุภาพเมื่อเข้าสักการะ"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "เป็นศาลเจ้าแรกของอำเภอตะกั่วป่า และมีการเชิญองค์เทพจากเมืองจีนมาประดิษฐาน ตามเอกสารสภาวัฒนธรรม นายหง่อจกซื้อบ้านเลขที่ 87 ถนนศรีตะกั่วป่ามาทำเป็นศาลเจ้า หลังขอพรเรื่องผลผลิตเหมืองแร่และโชคลาภ"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "มีองค์เทพนาจาและองค์เทพอื่น ๆ สำหรับสักการะ เอกสารชุมชนเล่าความเชื่อมโยงของศาลเจ้ากับการขอพรให้ทำเหมืองแร่ได้แร่ดีและมีกำไร ในเทศกาลกินเจมีพิธีโก้ยห่าน ข้ามสะพาน และผูกสายสิญจน์เพื่อความเป็นสิริมงคล"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/kue-chai/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/kue-chai/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/kue-chai/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/kue-chai/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Shrines & Vegetarian Halls</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place record · Shrines and vegetarian halls</span><h1>Kue Chai Tung Shrine</h1><p class="english">Kue Chai Tung Shrine</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">9 items verified</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="kue-chai">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/kue-chai.webp" alt="ศาลเจ้ากู่ใช่ตึ๋ง" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8265089587, 98.3647240165 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8265089587,98.3647240165" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd>Dress politely when entering for worship. <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://anyflip.com/tshcu/hnol/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://www.thairath.co.th/news/local/south/1105465" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>From Mr. Ngo Chok's house to Takua Pa's first shrine</h3><p class="era-years">No verified construction year is available; some contemporary documents state that it is nearly 200 years old</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The starting point with the clearest evidence is not a year, but a community story: Mr. Ngo Chok bought house number 87 on Sri Takua Pa Road and converted it into a shrine, driven by faith after praying for tin mining yields and fortune. Another document refers to its original name as 'Thian Wan Keng' and its legal name as 'Kue Chai Tung'.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://anyflip.com/tshcu/hnol/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สภาวัฒนธรรมตำบลตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Sub-district Cultural Council), Takua Pa Vegetarian Festival</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>The shrine grew with the mining town and became a community ritual space</h3><p class="era-years">No year has been found for a change of ownership, restoration, or a tsunami event specifically verified for this site</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The context of the shrine is tied to Hokkien Chinese who immigrated to mine tin in Takua Pa and brought deities from China to be enshrined. Local sources and travel media explain that the shrine is in the old market district, which has old buildings and a cultural street. It therefore serves as more than a place to pray: it is an anchor for the Chinese community and a space for the Vegetarian Festival.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</a> · <a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takua Pa Old Town boundary delineation project</a> · <a href="https://wanderlog.com/th/place/details/11412698/san-chao-ku-chai-tueng" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wanderlog (place information summary/user reviews)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A northern shrine still alive during the Vegetarian Festival</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The latest evidence found is NBT news published in May 2026 (2569 B.E.), which presents Kue Chai Tung Shrine, or 'Rong Phra Talat Nuea' (the northern market shrine), as a center of faith for Takua Pa people and states that it still preserves its original cultural identity. News of the 2023 festival also confirms that Kue Chai Tung Shrine participated in the Iu Keng ceremony, parading deities around the old town of Takua Pa.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q6K2Zl6700I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NBT2HD</a> · <a href="https://www.innews.news/news.php?n=48726" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Innews</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">13 to 21 October 2015 (B.E. 2558)</p><h3>Ko Teng pole raising ceremony in the Vegetarian Festival</h3><p>There is a ceremony to invite the 9 lanterns and the presiding deities of the Vegetarian Festival.</p><a href="https://www.sanook.com/news/1881366/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">23 October 2023 (พ.ศ. 2566)</p><h3>Participating in the Ew Keng street procession around the old town</h3><p>Kue Chai Tung Shrine joined Sin Chai Tung Guan Yu Shrine in the street procession ceremony during the Vegetarian Festival.</p><a href="https://www.innews.news/news.php?n=48726" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">4 May 2026 (พ.ศ. 2569)</p><h3>Appeared in NBT news as a centre of faith</h3><p>NBT news presented the shrine as Rong Phra Talat Nuea and mentioned its history of over 200 years, but did not provide the exact founding year.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q6K2Zl6700I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Mr. Ngo Chok bought a house to make a shrine</h3><p>The Cultural Council documents state that house number 87 on Sri Takua Pa Road was turned into a shrine after praying for mining yields and good fortune.</p><a href="https://anyflip.com/tshcu/hnol/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Inviting deities from China to be enshrined</h3><p>The shrine is recorded as the first shrine in Takua Pa district. It has the deity Nezha and other deities for worship.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Chinese deities</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>There is the deity Nezha and other deities for worship.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Traces of a mining community</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Community documents recount the shrine's connection to praying for good tin yields and profit.</p><a href="https://anyflip.com/tshcu/hnol/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Bridge crossing ceremony</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>During the Vegetarian Festival, there is a Koi Han ceremony (crossing a bridge to ward off bad luck) and the tying of holy thread for auspiciousness.</p><a href="https://www.thairath.co.th/news/local/south/1105465" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa old town context</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located in the cultural street and old town district of Takua Pa, which features old buildings and community arts and culture.</p><a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1097396" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2026-05-04 · NBT2HD</p><h3>Praying for blessings at Kue Chai Tung Shrine, Phang Nga Province</h3><p>NBT news recommended the shrine and its role as a centre of faith for Takua Pa people.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q6K2Zl6700I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2023-10-23 · Innews</p><h3>Fierce finale! Phang Nga Vegetarian Festival procession around Takua Pa city</h3><p>Reported on the Ew Keng ceremony where Kue Chai Tung Shrine joined Sin Chai Tung Shrine.</p><a href="https://www.innews.news/news.php?n=48726" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The name 'Rong Phra Talat Nuea' (northern market shrine) is used to distinguish this shrine from Sin Chai Tung Shrine, or the southern market shrine, in the old town district.</p><a href="https://th.readme.me/p/44374" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>This shrine was originally named Thian Wan Keng, and community documents state its legal name is Kue Chai Tung.</p><a href="https://anyflip.com/tshcu/hnol/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located in the old town district of Takua Pa, on Sri Takua Pa Road. The sources read do not specify the distance or detailed route recommendations.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No readable sources have been found that specify the direct route or distance to the shrine.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No readable sources have been found that specify the direct route or distance to the shrine.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No readable sources have been found that specify the direct route or distance to the shrine.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li><a href="/en/places/guan-yu/">Guan Yu / Sin Chai Tung Shrine</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/pun-thao/">Pun Thao Kong A Shrine</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/rong-jae/">The Shrine in the Garden</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>How to dress</summary><p>Dress politely when entering for worship.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>It is the first shrine in Takua Pa District, with deities invited from China to be enshrined here. According to Cultural Council documents, Ngo Chok bought house number 87 on Thanon Si Takua Pa and turned it into a shrine after praying for good mining yields and good fortune.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>It houses Na Cha and other deities for worship. Community documents link the shrine to prayers for good ore and profitable mining. During the Vegetarian Festival, the shrine holds the Koi Han ceremony, a bridge-crossing ritual, and a sacred-thread tying ritual for good fortune.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4411" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สภาวัฒนธรรมตำบลตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Sub-district Cultural Council), Takua Pa Vegetarian Festival</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://anyflip.com/tshcu/hnol/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Thairath</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.thairath.co.th/news/local/south/1105465" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">TAT Media Assets</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1097396" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Takua Pa Old Town boundary delineation project</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Innews</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.innews.news/news.php?n=48726" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">NBT2HD</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q6K2Zl6700I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Trip.com Moments</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://th.trip.com/moments/detail/takua-pa-14944-125098619/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>No opening and closing times found from verifiable sources.</li><li>Verified admission fees could not be found.</li><li>No official phone number, Facebook page, website, or LINE account for the shrine found.</li><li>No postal code specific to the location found from readable sources.</li><li>No verifiable data on the exact construction year or names of builders.</li><li>No evidence found of registration as an ancient monument by the Fine Arts Department.</li><li>No verifiable data on the Sino-Portuguese or Chinese architectural style of the building itself.</li><li>No verifiable data found for parking, restrooms, ramps, or wheelchair access.</li><li>No list of nearby places with verified walking times found.</li><li>No routes or distances from Phuket, Khao Lak, or the airport that specify this shrine directly found.</li><li>No specific construction year or verifiable evidence of builders other than the Mr. Ngo Chok story found.</li><li>No verifiable evidence of a change of hands, abandonment, or restoration with years found.</li><li>No evidence found that the shrine was affected by the 2004 tsunami.</li><li>No year of ancient monument registration by the Fine Arts Department found.</li><li>No information found on current caretakers, opening times, admission fees, structural condition, or recent restoration projects.</li><li>No old photos or archival photos verified to be this shrine directly found.</li><li>News from the past five years is limited; no news of restorations or awards specific to the location found.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
site\en\places\food-center\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Takua Pa Open-Air Food Center · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="Used as a starting point to explore local food in the town · Takua Pa Food Center · Lan Long Market Takua Pa · Takuapa food court"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Takua Pa Open-Air Food Center"><meta property="og:description" content="Used as a starting point to explore local food in the town · Takua Pa Food Center · Lan Long Market Takua Pa · Takuapa food court"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/places/food-center/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/food-center.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/food-center.png"><meta name="generator" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/food-center/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "หน้าแรก", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "ศูนย์อาหารลานโล่งตะกั่วป่า · ตลาดลานโล่ง", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/places/food-center/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "TouristAttraction", "name": "ศูนย์อาหารลานโล่งตะกั่วป่า", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/food-center/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/food-center.webp", "description": "เอกสารแนะนำศูนย์อาหารที่รวมอาหารหลายประเภท", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "postalCode": "82110", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.8675924, "longitude": 98.3420033}}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "มีค่าเข้าชมหรือไม่", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ข้อมูลยังไม่ยืนยัน · วงในระบุว่าไม่มีค่าเข้าชมสำหรับผู้ใหญ่และเด็ก ยังไม่มีหลักฐานยืนยันจากผู้ดูแลตลาด"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "เดินทางจากตัวเมืองตะกั่วป่าอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ใช้ลานพระรูปพระนารายณ์เป็นจุดสังเกต: รีวิวร้านขนมจีนป้าม่อมระบุว่าร้านอยู่บริเวณลานโล่งฝั่งตรงข้าม ข้อมูลนี้เป็นจุดสังเกตจากรีวิว ไม่ใช่เส้นทางนำทางที่ตรวจสอบแล้ว"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "วิดีโอประชาสัมพันธ์ของเทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่าที่เผยแพร่วันที่ 1 กันยายน 2567 แนะนำตลาดลานโล่งเป็นแหล่งรวมอาหารหลายประเภท หลักฐานนี้ยืนยันการประชาสัมพันธ์ในปีดังกล่าว ไม่ใช่ปีสร้างตลาด ข่าววันที่ 19 มิถุนายน 2568 กล่าวถึงแนวทางพัฒนาตลาดลานโล่งเป็นศูนย์อาหารสมัยใหม่และเพิ่มทางเลือกอาหารริมทาง เป็นการรายงานแผนพัฒนา ไม่ใช่หลักฐานว่าโครงการแล้วเสร็จ"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "เทศบาลแนะนำว่ามีข้าวราดแกงและอาหารตามสั่งให้เลือกซื้อ อาหารเส้นสองประเภทนี้ปรากฏในรายการอาหารที่เทศบาลประชาสัมพันธ์ เทศบาลระบุว่ามีตัวเลือกขนม ของหวาน และเครื่องดื่มภายในตลาด"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/food-center/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/food-center/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/food-center/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/food-center/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Markets & Food</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Saved places · Markets and food</span><h1>Takua Pa Open-Air Food Center</h1><p class="english">Food Center</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">5 verified items</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="food-center">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/food-center.webp" alt="ศูนย์อาหารลานโล่งตะกั่วป่า" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8675924, 98.3420033 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8675924,98.3420033" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/ui/search.html?q=%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%82%E0%B8%A5%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%87" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd>08:00 to 22:00 according to the Takua Pa Town Municipality video description published on 1 September 2024. The current schedule and holidays are not verified, and Wongnai lists another set of hours as every day 03:00 to 21:00. <span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd>Wongnai states there is no admission fee for adults and children. There is still no confirmed evidence from the market management. <span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd>Wongnai states there is parking, but does not specify the number of spots, parking fees, or accessible parking for people with disabilities. <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://www.wongnai.com/attractions/399190Vq-ตลาดลานโล่ง" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>Starting year of the open-air market is not verified yet</h3><p class="era-years"></p><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p>The available online evidence does not yet state when the open-air market was first built, who built it, or which project it began as. It is therefore not yet possible to responsibly say that this place originated in the tin-mining era, the era of the provincial rulers, or the period of modern urban expansion.</p><p>Takua Pa's context only tells us that the town has roots in trade and mining, and that the market district is an important community area. There is still no direct evidence linking this food center to a specific role in the town during those periods. Replacing the site's history with the history of the old town therefore risks creating a story that goes beyond the sources.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning) · Takua Pa Old Town Boundary Demarcation Project</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>A food market that gradually became the town's dining spot</h3><p class="era-years">At least 2020 to 2025</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>A food-review source published in 2020 (B.E. 2563) identifies Ko Ek's shop as being “in Takua Pa Open-Air Market” and records it as open during the daytime. This confirms that the area was already functioning as a market with food shops at that time, not merely as an empty lot.</p><p>In 2024 (B.E. 2567), Takua Pa Town Municipality promoted the open-air market as a center for many types of food, from rice with curry, made-to-order dishes, noodles, and khanom chin to snacks and drinks. A 2025 news report discusses plans to develop it into a modern food center or food court. This is a development plan, not evidence that construction was completed. No evidence has been found that the market was affected by the 2004 tsunami, abandoned, or registered as an ancient monument.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://roijang.com/2020/05/28/dried-ricesoup-lanloang-tkp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Aroi Jung Phang Nga · Khao Tom Haeng at Ko X shop, Lan Long Market, Takua Pa</a> · <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) · Lan Long Market introduction video</a> · <a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/630235" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Siam Rath · Lan Long Market development guidelines news</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>Still a food hub, but the status of the new project requires following up</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p>The latest evidence found confirms that Lan Loeng Market existed during 2024 to 2025 (B.E. 2567 to 2568) and indicates that small vendors were still using the area to sell food. The municipality previously gave approximate opening hours of 08:00 to 22:00, but review platforms list a different schedule, so the current hours should not be treated as verified.</p><p>No 2026 (B.E. 2569) announcement has yet been found confirming the direct administrator, building condition, facilities, or opening to visitors as a tourist attraction. There is also no confirming evidence that the plan to upgrade it into a modern food center/food court has been completed. The safest overall description is that it is a food market used by the community and small vendors, with a development direction, while current details should still be checked again with the municipality.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) · Lan Long Market introduction video</a> · <a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/630235" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Siam Rath · Lan Long Market development guidelines news</a> · <a href="https://mgronline.com/daily/detail/9670000105538" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MGR Online · News on raw material prices and Lan Long Market vendors</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2020 (2563 BE)</p><h3>Lan Long Market has food stalls open for service</h3><p>A review of Go Ek shop stated its location in Lan Long Market and recorded its opening hours from 11:00 to 17:00, serving as evidence of the area's use as a food market.</p><a href="https://roijang.com/2020/05/28/dried-ricesoup-lanloang-tkp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1 September 2024 (B.E. 2567)</p><h3>Municipality promotes Lan Long Market as a food hub</h3><p>Takua Pa Town Municipality recommended multiple food groups and stated the hours as 08:00 to 22:00. This evidence confirms the promotion in that year, not the market's founding year.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">19 June 2025 (B.E. 2568)</p><h3>News on guidelines to upgrade the market into a modern food center</h3><p>News reported a guideline to develop it into a modern food center and food court, increasing street food choices, but it is not verified if the construction is completed.</p><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/630235" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Various main dishes</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The municipality recommends that there are curry on rice and made-to-order dishes available.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Noodles and Kanom Jeen</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>These two types of noodle dishes appear in the food list promoted by the municipality.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Desserts, sweets, and drinks</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The municipality notes that there are dessert, sweet, and drink options inside the market.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Kanom Jeen with side vegetables at Pa Mom's stall</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Reviews mention Pa Mom's Kanom Jeen stall in the open-air area, offering various curries and many side vegetables. The stall information comes from reviewers and the current menu is not verified.</p><a href="https://www.wongnai.com/reviews/c3794fae6e6d4db4bcfe9596b0bd6a2d" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2025-06-19 · Siam Rath</p><h3>Guideline to develop Lan Long Market into a modern food center</h3><p>News reported the market development plan and increased street food choices, while it is not verified if the construction is completed.</p><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/630235" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2024-11-01 · MGR Online</p><h3>Coconut costs affect Hor Mok prices in Lan Long Market</h3><p>News cited an example of a Ton Pho Hor Mok vendor in Lan Long Market adjusting prices due to higher coconut costs.</p><a href="https://mgronline.com/daily/detail/9670000105538" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2024-09-01 · Takua Pa Municipality (Takua Pa Municipality)</p><h3>Municipality invites eating at Lan Long Market</h3><p>Takua Pa Town Municipality published a video recommending the market and various types of food.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The name open-air market appears in online evidence since at least 2020 from local restaurant reviews.</p><a href="https://roijang.com/2020/05/28/dried-ricesoup-lanloang-tkp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The municipality describes the market as offering savory food, desserts, sweets, and drinks, but does not state the founding year.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Use the Phra Narai monument square as a landmark; reviews of Pa Mom's Kanom Jeen stall note that it is located in the open-air area opposite the square. This information is an observation from reviews, not a verified navigation route.</p><a href="https://www.wongnai.com/reviews/c3794fae6e6d4db4bcfe9596b0bd6a2d" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>Phra Narai Park <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://www.wongnai.com/attractions/399190Vq-ตลาดลานโล่ง" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/riverwalk/">Takuapa Riverwalk</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/culture-street/">Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Admission fee</summary><p>Not verified · Wongnai states that there is no admission fee for adults and children, but there is no confirmation from the market operator</p></details><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Use the Phra Narai monument square as a landmark; reviews of Pa Mom's Kanom Jeen stall note that it is located in the open-air area opposite the square. This information is an observation from reviews, not a verified navigation route.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>A promotional video from Takua Pa Municipality (Takua Pa Municipality), published on 1 September 2024 (B.E. 2567), presents Lan Loeng Market as a place offering many types of food. This evidence confirms promotion in that year, not the year the market was established. A report dated 19 June 2025 (B.E. 2568) discusses plans to develop Lan Loeng Market into a modern food court and add more street-food options. It reports a development plan, not evidence that the project was completed</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>The municipality recommends rice with curry and made-to-order dishes. These two types of noodle dishes appear in the food list promoted by the municipality. The municipality also says that snacks, desserts, and drinks are available in the market</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Takua Pa Municipality (Takua Pa Municipality) · What should we eat for lunch, and where? .. @Lan Loeng Market</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wongnai · Lan Loeng Market</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.wongnai.com/attractions/399190Vq-ตลาดลานโล่ง" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wongnai · Pa Mom Kanom Chin review</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.wongnai.com/reviews/c3794fae6e6d4db4bcfe9596b0bd6a2d" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Siam Rath · News on Takua Pa urban development plans, 19 June 2025 (B.E. 2568)</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/630235" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) · Lan Long Market introduction video</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBj0I_sMc-I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Aroi Jung Phang Nga · Khao Tom Haeng at Ko X shop, Lan Long Market, Takua Pa</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://roijang.com/2020/05/28/dried-ricesoup-lanloang-tkp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Siam Rath · Lan Long Market development guidelines news</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/630235" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">MGR Online · News on raw material prices and Lan Long Market vendors</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mgronline.com/daily/detail/9670000105538" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning) · Takua Pa Old Town Boundary Demarcation Project</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>The main Thai and English names follow the prompt; readable sources use the name open-air market. No source confirming the English name Food Center as official has been found. Search terms in both languages are suggestions for SEO, not search volume data.</li><li>No Google Maps, OpenStreetMap, Mapcarta, or Wikidata pins for the food center itself were found in verifiable sources, so individual stall or town center coordinates are not used as a substitute.</li><li>The street address, number, and subdistrict are not verified: Wongnai states Bang Nai Si subdistrict, but waterworks news search results state Takua Pa subdistrict and the content could not be accessed, so the subdistrict is left blank; the 82110 postal code is cited from Wongnai and is not verified with official sources.</li><li>Opening hours conflict: The municipality stated 08:00 to 22:00 in 2024 media, while Wongnai stated everyday 03:00 to 21:00.</li><li>No phone number, Facebook page, website, or LINE account verified as a direct channel for the food center was found, so vendor or reviewer channels are not used as substitutes.</li><li>Admission fee information is only from Wongnai, no official announcement found; current parking fees and availability are unknown.</li><li>No verified information on actively used restrooms, ramps, uneven floors, disabled restrooms, and conveniences for the elderly or wheelchairs was found.</li><li>No readable source specifies the route to the market from Phuket and Khao Lak, distance, fare, or bus schedules; landmarks from the town center are only from reviews, and full travel routes are not verified.</li><li>No construction year, creator, or founding history of the food center was found, including specific roles in the tin mining era, evidence of Chinese or Sino-Portuguese architectural styles, and historical site registration, so the old town's history is not tied to the market.</li><li>No best time to visit, duration, or dress code with location-specific evidence was found.</li><li>No regular food center festivals, event months, lunar calendar dates, or verified activities were found.</li><li>Wongnai states that Phra Narai Park is about 200 meters near the market, but does not state if it is a walking distance and does not verify pedestrian crossings, so walking time is not estimated.</li><li>An official municipality video was found, but a working still image link and usage rights have not been verified; publicly released photos or videos do not imply permission for reuse.</li><li>The food list references 2024 municipality media and reviews, not a survey of actually open vendors on the research day.</li><li>No evidence specifying the starting year, founder, land-owning agency, or reason for establishing the market was found.</li><li>No evidence directly connecting the open-air market to the tin mining era, maritime trade, Hokkien Chinese, or the governor system was found.</li><li>No evidence that the market was abandoned, changed hands, restored, or damaged by the 2004 tsunami was found.</li><li>No evidence of historical site registration or use of the location for other activities in the past was found.</li><li>The operational status, caretaker, area condition, restrooms, parking, and current opening hours in 2026 still need verification with the municipality.</li><li>No image URL with directly verifiable rights has been found yet; if photos from other pages or websites are found, permission must be requested before use when rights are unknown.</li><li>The MGR Online news date uses the 2024 context of the article, but the accessible webpage does not show the date in readable lines, so it should be double-checked before publishing.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
