"name": "ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/riverwalk/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/riverwalk.webp", "description": "พื้นที่ตลาดริมแม่น้ำที่มีสินค้าและอาหารท้องถิ่น", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "ถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า/ถนนริมคลอง ข้างวัดย่านยาว", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "postalCode": "82110", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.87157, "longitude": 98.35091}}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "เปิดให้เข้าชมเวลาใด", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ข้อมูลยังไม่ยืนยัน · วันเสาร์ 15:00 ถึง 20:00 น."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีค่าเข้าชมหรือไม่", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ข้อมูลยังไม่ยืนยัน · ไม่มีค่าธรรมเนียมการเข้าชม"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "เดินทางจากตัวเมืองตะกั่วป่าอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "เดินทางไปย่านริมน้ำ/ถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า บริเวณข้างวัดย่านยาว; แหล่งข้อมูลระบุว่าสามารถใช้รถรับจ้างท้องถิ่นหรือมอเตอร์ไซค์รับจ้างจากสถานีขนส่งตะกั่วป่าได้"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ตลาดมีชื่อในโครงการตลาดประชารัฐต้องชมว่า ‘ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า ร่วมใจประชารัฐ’ และตั้งอยู่ถนนริมคลองข้างวัดย่านยาว"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "มีแผงจำหน่ายขนมพื้นบ้าน อาหารพื้นเมือง สินค้าโอทอป และของดีเมืองตะกั่วป่า ตลาดตั้งอยู่ติดแนวคลอง/แม่น้ำตะกั่วป่า เหมาะกับการชมวิวริมน้ำและถ่ายภาพ รีวิวผู้ใช้ระบุว่ามีดนตรีสดโดยนักเรียนในบางช่วง"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/riverwalk/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/riverwalk/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/riverwalk/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/riverwalk/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Markets & Food</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Saved places · Markets and food</span><h1>Takuapa Riverwalk</h1><p class="english">Takuapa Riverwalk</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">9 items verified</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="riverwalk">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" width="264" height="282" alt="ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า" loading="eager"><figcaption>Archive photograph: boats moored at the Takua Pa landing<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.87157, 98.35091 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.87157,98.35091" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://mapcarta.com/W816145865" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd>Saturdays, 3:00 PM to 8:00 PM <span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd>Free admission <span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><span class="source-offline">Visitor information sources ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span><a href="https://www.thai-tour.com/place/phangnga/takuapa/4206" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://wanderlog.com/place/details/11412806/takuapa-river-market" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#gallery">Gallery</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#nearby-note"></a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>From a mining town port to a riverside market space</h3><p class="era-years">No founding year has been found for the present market; old-town context: 1782 to the early 20th Buddhist century</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Available evidence describes the history of the Takua Pa town area and the pier, rather than specifying the exact origin of this riverside market. Takua Pa has been a port town and a centre for goods exchange since ancient times, before growing from tin mining and water trade. The old town is situated in a location surrounded by rivers on three sides, making it suitable for navigation, trade, and town defence.</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" width="264" height="282" alt="ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Archive photograph: boats moored at the Takua Pa landing<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</a> · <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Talat Yai Community</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>When mining slowed, the pier became a memory and was then revived</h3><p class="era-years">Around the 1970s to 2019 (B.E. 2520 to 2562)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>In the later period, the area was revitalised in the form of a community market under the name "Takuapa Riverwalk Ruamjai Pracharat". A Department of Internal Trade document with data as of 31 January 2019 (2562 BE) specified its location next to Wat Yan Yao (a local temple) and opening hours on Saturdays from 15:00 to 20:00. Evidence has not verified if the market was directly impacted by the 2004 tsunami or registered as a historical site under the market's name.</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" width="264" height="282" alt="ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Archive photograph: boats moored at the Takua Pa landing<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">References · <span class="source-offline">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce) <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A Saturday canal side market that brings old town memories back to life</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p>The market is located in the old town landscape featuring Chinese and Sino-Portuguese buildings. Riverside activities by the municipality still appear in planning documents, such as almsgiving along the river next to Wat Nikornwararam (Wat Yan Yao), and the Ministry of Culture lists a seafood festival specifying the market as the venue. However, the name of the agency or person directly managing the market has not been verified, nor have permanent restoration projects for the market itself in 2026.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gplace</a> · <a href="https://www.thai-tour.com/place/phangnga/takuapa/4206" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Thai-tour</a> · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_strategy/2022-12_231dcd9d5169573.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takua Pa Town Municipality: Development Plan Monitoring Report</a> · <a href="https://calendar.m-culture.go.th/events/103651" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ปฏิทินวัฒนธรรม กระทรวงวัฒนธรรม (Cultural Calendar, Ministry of Culture)</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1809 (พ.ศ. 2352)</p><h3>Original town destroyed by the Burmese and people migrated</h3><p>The original Takua Pa town was destroyed and abandoned before being revived around Ban Talat Yai during the reign of King Rama III.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2018 (พ.ศ. 2561)</p><h3>Market listed in the Must-See Market project</h3><p>Government documents name the Takua Pa Riverside Market, Ruam Jai Pracharath in Phang Nga province.</p><a href="https://einspection.moc.go.th/th/file/get/file/20210720dcb8f52155b576a7ca523b2a2247e871134559.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Information as of 31 January 2019 (พ.ศ. 2562)</p><h3>Official location and time data available</h3><p>The Department of Internal Trade states that the market is located on the canal-side road next to Wat Yan Yao and opens on Saturdays from 3:00 PM to 8:00 PM.</p><span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Takua Pa grew into a port and trade center</h3><p>The riverside area was the axis for navigation, goods exchange, and settlements of people from various nations.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Chap Se area served as an old port</h3><p>The name Chap Se is a Hokkien Chinese word meaning port, and is associated with the Chinese merchant community and the tin mining economy.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Mines gradually closed, town shifted from a mining hub to an old town</h3><p>Local historical sources note that prosperity from mining declined after the mines gradually closed, and the river became shallow due to mining sediment.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Seafood festival uses the market as a venue</h3><p>The Ministry of Culture's cultural calendar lists the Takua Pa Seafood Festival at the riverside market, although accessible pages do not clearly show the event dates.</p><a href="https://calendar.m-culture.go.th/events/103651" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><section class="research-section" id="gallery"><h2>Gallery</h2><div data-gallery><div class="gallery-tabs" hidden><button type="button" data-tab="today">Present photos</button><button type="button" data-tab="archive">Historical photos</button></div><div id="gallery-today" data-panel="today"><h3>Present photos</h3><div class="photo-grid"><p class="muted">No images authorized for publication in this category yet</p></div></div><div id="gallery-archive" data-panel="archive"><h3>Historical photos</h3><div class="photo-grid"><figure class="research-photo"><a data-lightbox href="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" aria-label="ขยายภาพ · ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" width="264" height="282" alt="ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Archive photograph: boats moored at the Takua Pa landing<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></div></div></section><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Local food and snacks</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Stalls selling local sweets, native food, OTOP products, and Takua Pa's specialities.</p><a href="https://www.thai-tour.com/place/phangnga/takuapa/4206" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Canal side atmosphere</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The market is located along the Takua Pa canal or river, suitable for river viewing and photography.</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Performances and music</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>User reviews indicate there is live music by students at times.</p><a href="https://wanderlog.com/place/details/11412806/takuapa-river-market" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Connecting to the old town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located near Takua Pa old town and the Sino-Portuguese buildings of the Talat Yai community.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The term "Chap Se" used for the old commercial district is related to a Hokkien Chinese word and the old Takua Pa pier.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Takua Pa old town has evidence of water trade with merchant ships from China and Myanmar.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Travel to the riverside area or Sri Takuapa Road near Wat Yan Yao. Sources suggest using local hired vehicles or motorcycle taxis from the Takua Pa bus terminal.</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance to the market found from readable sources</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance to the market found from readable sources</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance to the market found from readable sources</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>Wat Yan Yao (Wat Nikorn Wararam) <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></li><li>Takua Pa old town / Talat Yai community <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li>Takua Pa bus terminal <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://mapcarta.com/W816145865" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/culture-street/">Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/food-center/">Takua Pa Open-Air Food Center</a></li></ul></section><aside class="nearby-note"><span class="chapter">Stop nearby</span><p>If you want to sit and rest after walking through the market, the old market area is not far away. An old wooden house on Thanon Rat Bamrung is open as a café.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://siwaracafe.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">A place to sit near the market ↗</a></aside><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Opening hours</summary><p>Not verified · Saturdays, 15:00 to 20:00</p></details><details><summary>Admission fee</summary><p>Not verified · No admission fee</p></details><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Travel to the riverside area or Sri Takuapa Road near Wat Yan Yao. Sources suggest using local hired vehicles or motorcycle taxis from the Takua Pa bus terminal.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>The market is named 'Takua Pa Riverside Market, Ruam Jai Pracharath' in the Must-See Pracharath Market project and is located on the canal-side road next to Wat Yan Yao.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>Stalls sell local sweets, regional food, OTOP products, and goods from Takua Pa. The market sits beside the canal·Takua Pa River, making it suitable for riverside views and photography. User reviews say students sometimes perform live music.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><span class="source-offline">Open source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Mapcarta (OpenStreetMap data)</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mapcarta.com/W816145865" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Thai-tour</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.thai-tour.com/place/phangnga/takuapa/4206" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Gplace</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Talat Yai Community</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/index.php/site/detail/4431" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wanderlog</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wanderlog.com/place/details/11412806/takuapa-river-market" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_strategy/2022-12_231dcd9d5169573.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ปฏิทินวัฒนธรรม กระทรวงวัฒนธรรม (Cultural Calendar, Ministry of Culture)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://calendar.m-culture.go.th/events/103651" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Muang Boran Journal</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Ministry of Commerce: Must-See Markets in Southern Thailand</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://einspection.moc.go.th/th/file/get/file/20210720dcb8f52155b576a7ca523b2a2247e871134559.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Coordinates with a specific riverside market sign were not found, so market or nearby coordinates from OpenStreetMap via Mapcarta are used.</li><li>Phone number, Facebook page, website, or official LINE of the market not found.</li><li>Evidence confirming the founding year, creator, or historical site registration of the market not found.</li><li>Verified data on parking, restrooms, access for the elderly or wheelchairs, and dress code not found.</li><li>Festivals specific to the market not verified.</li><li>Official image links with specified usage rights are not verified.</li><li>Evidence specifying the first opening year, founder, responsible person, or owner agency of the market not found.</li><li>Evidence of the market being abandoned, restored, or changing hands during any period not found.</li><li>Evidence verifying direct impact from the 2004 tsunami on the market area not found.</li><li>Evidence of the riverside market being registered as a historical site not found; registrations found belong to other elements in the old town.</li><li>Latest market opening announcement for 2026 from direct caretakers not found, so current opening days and times cannot be verified yet.</li><li>News from the past 5 years specifying direct market restoration or development projects with clear publication dates not found.</li><li>Old photos identified directly as the riverside market area not found.</li><li>All photos are links from online travel sources with unknown rights, requiring permission before use.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
site\en\places\wat-nikorn\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Wat Nikornwararam · Wat Yanyao, Takua Pa · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="Retelling the site&#x27;s history through its role in the community · Takuapa temple · Phang Nga temple · old temple in Takuapa"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Wat Nikornwararam · Wat Yanyao, Takua Pa"><meta property="og:description" content="Retelling the site&#x27;s history through its role in the community · Takuapa temple · Phang Nga temple · old temple in Takuapa"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-nikorn/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/wat-nikorn.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/wat-nikorn.png"><meta name="generator" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/wat-nikorn/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Wat Nikornwararam (Wat Yan Yao) · Wat Takua Pa", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-nikorn/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "TouristAttraction", "name": "Wat Nikornwararam (Wat Yan Yao)", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-nikorn/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/wat-nikorn.webp", "description": "Documents link the temple with the community and the 2004 tsunami (พ.ศ. 2547).", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "Yan Yao village, Thanon Phet Kasem", "addressLocality": "Takua Pa", "addressRegion": "Phang Nga", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.8691760396, "longitude": 98.348042969}}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "How should visitors dress?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Dress respectfully when entering a religious site."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the history of this place?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The temple was built in 1793 (พ.ศ. 2336) by Khun Ta Kaew and Khun Ta Ram. It received royal consecration of its ecclesiastical boundary in 1842 (พ.ศ. 2385)."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is there to see?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Confirmed highlights are its founding in 1793 (พ.ศ. 2336) and royal consecration of its ecclesiastical boundary in 1842 (พ.ศ. 2385). The temple was once used to gather victims’ remains while they awaited identity verification."}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-nikorn/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/wat-nikorn/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-nikorn/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/wat-nikorn/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Temples & Pagodas</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place record · Temples and pagodas</span><h1>Wat Nikornwararam</h1><p class="english">Wat Nikornwararam</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">9 items verified</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="wat-nikorn">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/wat-nikorn.webp" alt="วัดนิกรวราราม (วัดย่านยาว)" width="1000" height="726" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8691760396, 98.348042969 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8691760396,98.348042969" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4416" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd>Polite dress is recommended when entering the religious site. <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>A community temple in early Takua Pa</h3><p class="era-years">1793 to 1842 (พ.ศ. 2336 to 2385)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Wat Nikon Wararam, or Wat Yan Yao, was initially built in 1793 (2336 BE) by Khun Ta Kaew and Khun Ta Ram. The discovered evidence verifies the year and the names of the founders, but does not provide detailed reasons on what specific mission the temple was established for. Therefore, it should be viewed as a religious site of the local community forming in the Takua Pa basin, rather than tying it to stories without direct evidence.</p><p>The broader picture of Takua Pa town has a history as a port town and tin mining source, with maritime trade and various groups of people. However, no temple-specific evidence has been found to verify the role of Wat Nikon Wararam regarding tin mines, maritime trade, Hokkien Chinese people, or the governor system. Thus, no conclusions are made beyond the data sources.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4416" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Samnakngan Noyobai lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning) · Conserved Cultural Environment Sites</a> · <a href="https://anyflip.com/vlkdm/ecrk/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takola in the past... Takua Pa in the present</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>From an ancient temple to a tsunami memorial and land management</h3><p class="era-years">1842 to 2022 (พ.ศ. 2385 to 2565)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The temple received the royal granting of the land for a temple in 1842 (2385 BE), which is a crucial piece of evidence that the religious site was certified as an area for monastic activities according to the Sangha's tradition at the time. However, no documents have been found specifying major restorations, changes in ownership, or periods of abandonment.</p><p>After the tsunami on December 26, 2004 (2547 BE), the temple was used as a gathering place for the bodies of disaster victims awaiting forensic identification. This temporary role made Wat Yan Yao a part of Takua Pa's disaster response history. Later, on October 30, 2022 (2565 BE), the Samnakngan Phraphutthasatsana Changwat Phangnga (Phang Nga Provincial Office of Buddhism) participated in handing over the land title deed document to the abbot, serving as evidence of land ownership management in the modern era.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4416" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</a> · <a href="https://pna.onab.go.th/th/content/page/index/id/34431" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Samnakngan Phraphutthasatsana Changwat Phangnga (Phang Nga Provincial Office of Buddhism) · Handing over land title deed document</a> · <a href="https://www.cifs.go.th/Files/news/file/ff82ea76-112f-4392-a8ff-e485e9fbc04e.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sathaban Niti Witthayasat (Central Institute of Forensic Science) · Event record on December 28, 2004 (2547 BE)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A temple still serving as a centre for faith and public works</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The latest discovered evidence verifies that the temple is still in use, with Phra Khru Nikon Thammasophit as the abbot, and has monks in residence during the Buddhist Lent. The temple database indicates the organization of the united Kathina ceremony in 2024 (2567 BE) and 2025 (2568 BE), while government/local news verifies the temple's participation in district and provincial level activities.</p><p>In recent years, the temple has been both a space for religious activities and a public space: in 2024 (2567 BE) it was used as a donation center to help northern flood victims, and there was an inspection visit for the Temple, People, State, Creating Happiness project as a southern regional model temple. However, no data has been found verifying the opening and closing hours for tourists, detailed building conditions, or temple-specific restoration projects in 2026 (2569 BE).</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://pna.onab.go.th/th/content/page/index/id/34431" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานพระพุทธศาสนาจังหวัดพังงา (Phang Nga Provincial Office of Buddhism)</a> · <a href="https://www.dmc.tv/wat/13166" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DMC · 10,000 Temples United Kathina Project across Thailand</a> · <a href="https://archive.siamrath.co.th/n/568331" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Siam Rath · Donation center to help flood victims</a> · <a href="https://www.ride-explorer.com/?p=7378" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ride Explorer · Model temple inspection visit</a> · <a href="https://www.topnews.co.th/news/1546452" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TOPNEWS · Preserving Takua Pa old town Songkran festival</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1793 (2336 BE)</p><h3>Beginning of temple construction</h3><p>Khun Ta Kaeo and Khun Ta Ram built Wat Nikornwararam.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4416" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1842 (2385 BE)</p><h3>Received Wisungkhammasima</h3><p>The temple was granted Wisungkhammasima.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4416" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">December 26, 2004 (2547 BE)</p><h3>Post tsunami memorial area</h3><p>Used to gather bodies of victims waiting for identity verification.</p><a href="https://www.cifs.go.th/Files/news/file/ff82ea76-112f-4392-a8ff-e485e9fbc04e.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">October 30, 2022 (2565 BE)</p><h3>Received land title deed documents</h3><p>The Phang Nga Provincial Office of Buddhism and the Land Office handed over the title deed documents to the abbot.</p><a href="https://pna.onab.go.th/th/content/page/index/id/34431" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">September 22, 2024 (2567 BE)</p><h3>Donation center for northern floods</h3><p>The temple, together with the monastic community and the people of Takua Pa, collected items to help flood victims.</p><a href="https://archive.siamrath.co.th/n/568331" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2025 (2568 BE)</p><h3>Participated in Takua Pa old town Songkran event</h3><p>The abbot and monks of Wat Nikornwararam participated in the alms offering activity organized by the province.</p><a href="https://www.topnews.co.th/news/1546452" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>An ancient temple of the Yan Yao community</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Confirmed highlights include its establishment in 1793 CE (2336 BE) and receiving its royal boundary in 1842 CE.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4416" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>A space of tsunami memory</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The temple was used to gather the bodies of tsunami victims awaiting identification.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4416" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2025-04-13 · TOPNEWS</p><h3>Phang Nga continues Songkran traditions with alms offering in Takua Pa old town</h3><p>Phra Khru Nikorn Thammasophit and monks from Wat Nikornwararam participated in provincial activities.</p><a href="https://www.topnews.co.th/news/1546452" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2025-01-01 · Ride Explorer</p><h3>Inspection of the Temple, Public, State, Creating Happiness project</h3><p>Wat Nikornwararam was mentioned as a temple ready for southern regional assessment.</p><a href="https://www.ride-explorer.com/?p=7378" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2024-09-22 · Siam Rath</p><h3>Phang Nga monks unite to help flood victims in the north</h3><p>The temple set up a donation center for items together with the monastic community and the public.</p><a href="https://archive.siamrath.co.th/n/568331" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2022-10-30 · Samnakngan Phraphutthasatsana Changwat Phangnga (Phang Nga Provincial Office of Buddhism)</p><h3>Phang Nga Provincial Office of Buddhism joins in handing over the land title deed documents of Wat Nikornwararam</h3><p>Handing over the land title deed documents to Phra Khru Nikorn Thammasophit, the abbot of Wat Nikornwararam.</p><a href="https://pna.onab.go.th/th/content/page/index/id/34431" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Wat Yan Yao was used as a gathering place for the bodies of 2004 CE tsunami victims awaiting identification.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4416" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>In 2024 CE, the temple served as a donation centre to help flood victims in the North.</p><a href="https://archive.siamrath.co.th/n/568331" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No verified route recommendations were found from the available sources.</p></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No verified route recommendations were found from the available sources.</p></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No verified route recommendations were found from the available sources.</p></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No verified route recommendations were found from the available sources.</p></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>Takua Pa Riverside Market, Yan Yao Walking Street <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZeycJnHU_Nw" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-boromthat/">Wat Boromthat Khiri Khet (the town's relic temple)</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-khuha/">Wat Khuha Phimuk (the cave hill temple)</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-pathum/">Wat Pathum Thara (the front town temple)</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-kongkha/">Wat Kongkha Phimuk (the riverside temple)</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-sena/">Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>How to dress</summary><p>Polite dress is recommended when entering the religious site.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>The temple was built in 1793 (2336 BE) by Khun Ta Kaew and Khun Ta Ram. The temple received the royal granting of the land for a temple in 1842 (2385 BE).</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>Verified highlights are its founding history in 1793 (2336 BE) and receiving the royal granting of the land for a temple in 1842 (2385 BE). The temple was used to gather bodies of disaster victims awaiting forensic identification.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning) (ONEP) · Conserved Cultural Art Sites</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4416" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wat Nikon Wararam · ClassStart Books</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://books.classstart.org/thai-buddhist-temples/03/%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B4%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A1.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Strolling and eating at Takua Pa riverside market, Yan Yao walking street · YouTube</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZeycJnHU_Nw" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Samnakngan Noyobai lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning) · Conserved Cultural Environment Sites</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4416" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานพระพุทธศาสนาจังหวัดพังงา (Phang Nga Provincial Office of Buddhism)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://pna.onab.go.th/th/content/page/index/id/34431" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สถาบันนิติวิทยาศาสตร์ (Central Institute of Forensic Science) · Tsunami incident record</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.cifs.go.th/Files/news/file/ff82ea76-112f-4392-a8ff-e485e9fbc04e.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">DMC · Wat Nikornwararam</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.dmc.tv/wat/13166" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สยามรัฐ (Siam Rath) · Flood-relief donation center</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://archive.siamrath.co.th/n/568331" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">TOPNEWS · Songkran in Takua Pa Old Town</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.topnews.co.th/news/1546452" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Ride Explorer · Southern regional model temple</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.ride-explorer.com/?p=7378" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Takola in the past... Takua Pa in the present</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://anyflip.com/vlkdm/ecrk/basic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Verified opening hours could not be found from the read sources.</li><li>Verified admission fees, phone numbers, Facebook pages, websites, or LINE accounts could not be found.</li><li>A verified postcode could not be found, and secondary sources list a different subdistrict from official records.</li><li>No evidence confirms its role in the tin-mining era, Sino-Portuguese/Chinese architecture, or registration as a historical site.</li><li>Verified information on parking, restrooms, wheelchair access, and temple festivals could not be found.</li><li>Official image links with specified usage rights are not verified.</li><li>No temple-specific evidence confirms it was established for tin-mining activities, maritime trade, Hokkien Chinese, or the town governor system.</li><li>The year and details of restoration, abandonment, or historical site registration remain undiscovered.</li><li>Verified data on building conditions, restoration plans, opening hours, and annual activities in 2026 CE have not been found.</li><li>Due to conflicting subdistrict records in some sources, the official coordinates and lists from ONEP and the Phang Nga Provincial Office of Buddhism are used.</li><li>Some sources give conflicting subdistrict names, so the coordinates and official listings from สผ./สำนักงานพระพุทธศาสนาจังหวัดพังงา are treated as primary.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
site\en\places\wat-kongkha\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Wat Kongkha Phimuk · Wat Khongkha Takua Pa · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="Observing southern ordination hall lines · Khongkha Phimuk Temple · Takua Pa ancient temple · Phang Nga temple"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Wat Kongkha Phimuk · Wat Khongkha Takua Pa"><meta property="og:description" content="Observing southern ordination hall lines · Khongkha Phimuk Temple · Takua Pa ancient temple · Phang Nga temple"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-kongkha/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/wat-kongkha.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/wat-kongkha.png"><meta name="generator" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/wat-kongkha/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "หน้าแรก", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "วัดคงคาภิมุข (วัดคงคา) · วัดคงคาพิมุข", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-kongkha/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "TouristAttraction", "name": "วัดคงคาภิมุข (วัดคงคา)", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-kongkha/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/wat-kongkha.webp", "description": "มีอุโบสถแบบปักษ์ใต้ซึ่งเอกสารระบุว่าเป็นโบราณสถาน", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "ถนนราษฎร์บำรุง", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.840837, "longitude": 98.362899}, "telephone": "076-421-479"}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "เดินทางจากตัวเมืองตะกั่วป่าอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "จากที่ทำการเทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่าไปทางตะวันตกตามถนนเพชรเกษม/ทางหลวงหมายเลข 4 ราว 5 กิโลเมตร เลี้ยวซ้ายเข้าถนนราษฎร์บำรุง ตรงต่อประมาณ 280 เมตร แล้วเลี้ยวซ้ายตามทาง จะพบวัดอยู่ด้านขวามือ"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "อุโบสถและเจดีย์เป็นโบราณสถานที่ยังใช้งานอยู่ และวัดเป็นสถานปฏิบัติธรรมประจำจังหวัดพังงาแห่งที่ 1 กรมศิลปากรประกาศขึ้นทะเบียนโบราณสถานและกำหนดเขตที่ดินในราชกิจจานุเบกษาเมื่อ 18 ธันวาคม พ.ศ. 2539"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ชมอาคารก่ออิฐถือปูน หน้าบันและซุ้มประตูหน้าต่างประดับปูนปั้น รวมถึงภาพพระพุทธรูปและลวดลายพันธุ์พฤกษา เป็นหนึ่งในโบราณสถานสำคัญภายในวัดและยังอยู่ในวัดที่มีการใช้งาน วัดตั้งอยู่ริมฝั่งคลองตะกั่วป่าด้านตะวันตก โดยคลองอยู่ทางทิศตะวันออกของวัด"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-kongkha/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/wat-kongkha/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-kongkha/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/wat-kongkha/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Temples & Pagodas</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place record · Temples and pagodas</span><h1>Wat Kongkha Phimuk (the riverside temple)</h1><p class="english">Wat Kongkha Phimuk</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">6 items verified</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="wat-kongkha">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/wat-kongkha.webp" alt="วัดคงคาภิมุข (วัดคงคา)" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.840837, 98.362899 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.840837,98.362899" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd>OpenStreetMap data via Mapcarta indicates a wheelchair=yes tag, but details on ramp conditions or facilities from official sources are not verified. <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd>076-421-479 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://mapcarta.com/29028704" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Contact information ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>A riverside temple of Takua Pa, starting under the name 'Wat Kongkha'</h3><p class="era-years">1762 (B.E. 2305) (proposed by local and government sources); 1936 (B.E. 2479) (ordination hall)</p><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p>Evidence from the environmental art agency states the temple was built in 1762 (B.E. 2305) and originally named Wat “Kongkha”, while the archaeological database of Sun Manutsayawitthaya Sirindhorn (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre) indicates the age of the important historical site based on the ordination hall built in 1936 (B.E. 2479). The origin should therefore be read as a two-layer history: the temple's age according to registration or accounts, and the age of the surviving buildings, which are not the same.</p><p>The temple is located on an alluvial plain along Khlong Takua Pa, on the west side of the waterway, in a town with a history as a coastal city and a centre for tin mining and maritime trade. This urban context suggests the temple likely served as a religious site for the riverside community. However, no specific evidence for the temple has been found identifying the founder, the reason for construction, or the direct role of Hokkien Chinese or the town governor. Therefore, details beyond the evidence should not be added.</p><p>The ordination hall, built in 1936 (B.E. 2479), is a southern-style brick-and-mortar building facing east, decorated with stucco depicting pagodas, Buddha images, Dharma wheels, and flora. This reflects its role as both a space for religious ceremonies and a showcase of community craftsmanship from the late Rattanakosin period to the reign of King Rama VIII.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4417" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cultural Art Environment (ONEP)</a> · <a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ฐานข้อมูลแหล่งโบราณคดีที่สำคัญในประเทศไทย (ศมส.) (Important Archaeological Sites in Thailand Database, SAC)</a> · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) Environmental Operation Plan</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>A new name, a new historical site, and returning as a living temple</h3><p class="era-years">1940 (B.E. 2483); 1996 (B.E. 2539); 2002 (B.E. 2545)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The temple history recorded in the archaeological database states that it was originally called Wat Kongkha before being changed to Wat Kongkha Phimuk in 1940 (B.E. 2483). Meanwhile, the ordination hall and pagoda are still in use and have not become ruins isolated from the temple. The different names in documents should be preserved to show readers the site's development.</p><p>Krom Sinlapakon (Fine Arts Department) announced the registration of the ordination hall and pagoda, along with designating the historical site boundaries, in the Royal Gazette on 18 December 1996 (B.E. 2539). The registration ensures the heritage value of the old buildings is protected as an artistic legacy. Concurrently, it remains a private temple affiliated with the Maha Nikaya sect, with resident monks.</p><p>The provincial dharma practice centre registry of Samnakngan Phraphutthasatsana Haeng Chat (National Office of Buddhism) lists “Kongkha Phimuk” as the 1st dharma practice centre of Phang Nga province according to a 2002 (B.E. 2545) resolution. Currently, the archaeological database indicates that it is maintained and generally in stable condition. However, no evidence has been found verifying if the area was affected by the 2004 (B.E. 2547) tsunami or if it had a specific period of abandonment or restoration.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ฐานข้อมูลแหล่งโบราณคดีที่สำคัญในประเทศไทย (ศมส.) (Important Archaeological Sites in Thailand Database, SAC)</a> · <a href="https://www.onab.go.th/th/file/get/file/20230608fc490ca45c00b1249bbe3554a4fdf6fb104517.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานพระพุทธศาสนาแห่งชาติ (National Office of Buddhism) Provincial Meditation Center Registry</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A historical site that still breathes: An active temple and meditation center</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>In the latest published information, Wat Kongkha Phimuk still has resident monks and operates as a private temple affiliated with the Maha Nikaya sect. The maintaining agency is stated to be the temple itself, with the archaeological database advising to contact Phra Khru Nanthapanyakon, the abbot, at 076-421-479.</p><p>The ordination hall and pagoda are active historical sites. The temple interior is described as clean, shady, and suitable for religious practices. The temple also serves as the 1st provincial dharma practice centre of Phang Nga, making it a place where people can pay respects to Buddha, admire the stucco work, and engage in dharma practice.</p><p>Activities with cited sources include dharma practice in honour of the monarchy, overnight New Year prayers, Brahmin nun ordination for royal merit, and summer novice ordination. However, no 2026 (B.E. 2569) announcements have been found verifying activity schedules, opening hours, new restoration projects, or facility details. Therefore, you should call the temple before travelling.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ฐานข้อมูลแหล่งโบราณคดีที่สำคัญในประเทศไทย (ศมส.) (Important Archaeological Sites in Thailand Database, SAC)</a> · <a href="https://www.onab.go.th/th/file/get/file/20230608fc490ca45c00b1249bbe3554a4fdf6fb104517.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานพระพุทธศาสนาแห่งชาติ (National Office of Buddhism) Provincial Meditation Center Registry</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p class="era-years">1762 (B.E. 2305)</p><h3>Founding of Wat Kongkha (Data conflicts with building age evidence)</h3><p>ONEP states the temple was built in 1762 and originally named Wat Kongkha, but the archaeological database uses 1936 as the age of the ubosot, so it cannot be concluded whether the site and the building started in the same year.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4417" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1936 (B.E. 2479)</p><h3>Construction of the ubosot which is an important historical site</h3><p>The rectangular brick and mortar ubosot faces east and features stucco designs and southern Thai style roof structures.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p class="era-years">1940 (B.E. 2483)</p><h3>Renamed to Wat Kongkha Phimuk</h3><p>The temple history in the archaeological database states that it was originally named Wat Kongkha and then renamed to Wat Kongkha Phimuk.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">18 December 1996 (2539)</p><h3>Registered as a historical site</h3><p>The Fine Arts Department announced the registration of the historical site and defined the land area in the Royal Gazette Volume 113, Special Part 50 Ngor.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2002 (B.E. 2545)</p><h3>Became the first provincial meditation practice center of Phang Nga</h3><p>The National Office of Buddhism registry lists Wat Kongkha Phimuk as the first center of Phang Nga province according to resolution 12/2002.</p><a href="https://www.onab.go.th/th/file/get/file/20230608fc490ca45c00b1249bbe3554a4fdf6fb104517.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Historical site ordination hall</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>View the brick and stucco building. The gable and door or window arches are decorated with stucco art, including Buddha images and floral patterns.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Pagoda</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>It is one of the important historical sites within the temple and remains part of the active temple.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Atmosphere along the Takua Pa Canal</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The temple is located on the western bank of the Takua Pa Canal, with the canal situated to the east of the temple.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Stucco details on the gable</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The front features a pagoda, Buddha images in the gazing and alms-bowl holding postures, while the back features the Dharmachakra and a Naga-protected Buddha.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The name 'Kongkha Phimuk' appears as the first entry in the Phang Nga provincial meditation practice center register.</p><a href="https://www.onab.go.th/th/file/get/file/20230608fc490ca45c00b1249bbe3554a4fdf6fb104517.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The ordination hall and pagoda still serve as active historical sites and are not closed off merely as archaeological viewing spots.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>From the Takua Pa Town Municipality office, head west along Phetkasem Road / Highway 4 for about 5 kilometers, turn left onto Rat Bamrung Road, go straight for about 280 meters, then turn left along the path. The temple will be on the right.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>Somchai Andaman Building <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://mapcarta.com/29028704" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li>Kanda Supermarket <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://mapcarta.com/29028704" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-boromthat/">Wat Boromthat Khiri Khet (the town's relic temple)</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-khuha/">Wat Khuha Phimuk (the cave hill temple)</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-pathum/">Wat Pathum Thara (the front town temple)</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-nikorn/">Wat Nikornwararam</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-sena/">Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>From the Takua Pa Town Municipality office, head west along Phetkasem Road / Highway 4 for about 5 kilometers, turn left onto Rat Bamrung Road, go straight for about 280 meters, then turn left along the path. The temple will be on the right.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>The ordination hall and pagoda are active historical sites, and the temple serves as the first provincial meditation practice center of Phang Nga. The Fine Arts Department (Krom Sinlapakon) announced its registration as a historical site and defined its land boundaries in the Royal Gazette on December 18, 1996 (2539 BE).</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>Observe the brick and mortar building, with its pediment and arched doors and windows decorated with stucco, including Buddha images and floral patterns. It is one of the important historical sites within the temple and is still in an active temple. The temple is located on the west bank of Khlong Takua Pa, with the canal situated to the east of the temple.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">ฐานข้อมูลแหล่งโบราณคดีที่สำคัญในประเทศไทย (ศมส.) (Important Archaeological Sites in Thailand Database, SAC)</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cultural Art Environment (ONEP)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4417" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Mapcarta (Data from OpenStreetMap)</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mapcarta.com/29028704" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">TAT Media Assets</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1097442" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Thailand YellowPages</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.yellowpages.co.th/profile/%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%84%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%84%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A0%E0%B8%B4%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%82-nabHw5" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Samnakngan Phraphutthasatsana Haeng Chat (National Office of Buddhism)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.onab.go.th/th/file/get/file/20230608fc490ca45c00b1249bbe3554a4fdf6fb104517.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) Environmental Operation Plan</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Published and verified opening hours are not verified.</li><li>Admission fee data is not verified.</li><li>Facebook pages, websites, or LINE accounts confirmed to belong to the temple are not verified.</li><li>A postal code verified to match the temple from primary sources is not verified.</li><li>Routes and distances that can be verified from Phuket, Khao Lak, or the airport are not verified.</li><li>Data confirming the temple's role in the tin mining era is not verified.</li><li>Evidence confirming Sino-Portuguese or Chinese architecture is not verified.</li><li>Data confirming parking, restrooms, and recommended visit times are not verified.</li><li>Months or lunar calendar dates for the festivals are not verified.</li><li>Walking times to nearby places are not verified.</li><li>Evidence identifying the founder and reason for construction in 1762 is not verified.</li><li>Sources provide different years for the temple's start and the ordination hall's construction, so the temple's age cannot be summarized into a single year.</li><li>Evidence specifically for the temple regarding its role in tin mining, maritime trade, Hokkien Chinese, or the town ruler system is not verified.</li><li>Evidence confirming it was abandoned or damaged by the 2004 tsunami is not verified.</li><li>News from the past 5 years confirming renovation or development projects specifically for the temple are not verified.</li><li>Old photographs with verifiable sources are not verified.</li><li>A 2026 announcement regarding opening hours, activity schedules, and facilities is not verified.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
site\en\places\museum\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Takua Pa Community Museum · Takua Pa Museum · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="Connecting the story from old houses to the town&#x27;s memories · Wat Sena Nucharangsan · Takua Pa old town museum · Phang Nga local museum"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Takua Pa Community Museum · Takua Pa Museum"><meta property="og:description" content="Connecting the story from old houses to the town&#x27;s memories · Wat Sena Nucharangsan · Takua Pa old town museum · Phang Nga local museum"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/places/museum/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/museum.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/museum.png"><meta name="generator" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/museum/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "หน้าแรก", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "พิพิธภัณฑ์เสนานุชรังสรรค์ชุมชนตะกั่วป่า", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/places/museum/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "TouristAttraction", "name": "พิพิธภัณฑ์เสนานุชรังสรรค์ชุมชนตะกั่วป่า", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/museum/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/museum.webp", "description": "รวบรวมเรื่องศาสนา ศิลปะ และการค้าของท้องถิ่น", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "ภายในวัดเสนานุชรังสรรค์ ย่านตลาดเก่า", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "postalCode": "82110", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.8302299579, "longitude": 98.3624509671}}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "ควรแต่งกายอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ควรแต่งกายสุภาพเมื่อเข้าพื้นที่วัด"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "พิพิธภัณฑ์ชุมชนตะกั่วป่าเป็นอาคารสองชั้นภายในวัดเสนานุชรังสรรค์ และรวบรวมเครื่องใช้กับอุปกรณ์ที่สะท้อนวิถีชีวิตคนตะกั่วป่า รวมถึงของจากยุคเหมืองแร่ วัดเสนานุชรังสรรค์สร้างโดยพระยาเสนานุชิต (นุช) และอุโบสถมีอิทธิพลทางสถาปัตยกรรมจากจีน"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ตัวพิพิธภัณฑ์ชุมชนตั้งอยู่ภายในวัดเสนานุชรังสรรค์ จัดเก็บสิ่งของจากยุคทำเหมืองและของหายากที่สะท้อนวิถีชีวิตท้องถิ่น อุโบสถขนาดใหญ่มีรูปแบบได้รับอิทธิพลจากสถาปัตยกรรมจีน"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/museum/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/museum/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/museum/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/museum/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Museums</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place record · Museum</span><h1>Takua Pa Community Museum</h1><p class="english">Takua Pa Community Museum</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">8 items verified</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="museum">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/museum.webp" alt="พิพิธภัณฑ์เสนานุชรังสรรค์ชุมชนตะกั่วป่า" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8302299579, 98.3624509671 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8302299579,98.3624509671" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4412" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd>Modest attire is recommended when entering the temple grounds. <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9610000016873" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960255" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>Wat Mai Kamphaeng in a mining and port town</h3><p class="era-years">Since 1847 (B.E. 2390)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>This place began at Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan, formerly known by local residents as “Wat Mai Kamphaeng.” The temple register records its establishment in B.E. 2390 (1847), while local sources say it was built during the reign of King Rama III by Phraya Sena Nuchit (Nuch), governor of Takuapa.</p><p>At that time, Takuapa was an Andaman coastal port linking trade and tin resources. Various groups, especially workers and Chinese merchants, settled here, forming a market district and Chinese culture. The temple's Chinese-influenced ordination hall is therefore evidence of a multicultural town. For the museum seen today, no publicly available evidence identifies the year it was established or its direct founder.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.50amfh.org/userfiles/file/News/Thai%20temple%20name%20list/south/Phangnga.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Phang Nga Province temple registration report</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4412" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cultural environments for conservation (ONEP)</a> · <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Takua Pa Town</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>From a temple and community to a museum of memories</h3><p class="era-years">No establishment year for the museum has been found; evidence shows its use in the old-town context before 2018 (B.E. 2561).</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Over time, Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan has remained a religious site and community space. Meanwhile, Takuapa changed from a centre of tin mining and trade into a historic town preserving its heritage. Academic sources describe Takuapa Community Museum as a two-storey building displaying household items, equipment, and rare objects reflecting local life, including traces of the mining era.</p><p>The temple's ordination hall is registered as an ancient monument by the Fine Arts Department, but the sources verifiable this time do not clearly state the registration year. No evidence has been found that the museum building was abandoned, underwent major restoration, or was directly affected by the 2004 tsunami (B.E. 2547), so no conclusion is made beyond the evidence.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://so05.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/parichartjournal/article/download/219292/168797/871014" target="_blank" rel="noopener">วารสารปาริชาต มหาวิทยาลัยทักษิณ (Parichart Journal, Thaksin University)</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4412" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cultural environments for conservation (ONEP)</a> · <a href="https://www.andamannlttrang.com/%E0%B8%82%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B9%E0%B8%A5/%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B9%82%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%96%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%8A%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%A3/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สารสนเทศท้องถิ่นภาคใต้ฝั่งอันดามัน (Andaman Southern Thai Local Information)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A small museum on the old town route</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Contemporary sources call this place both “Takuapa Community Museum” and “Takuapa House Museum.” It is presented in the context of the old-town cultural street, displaying photographs, artefacts, and community stories alongside Sino-Portuguese buildings and old temples. Its role is therefore more that of a place for learning about the town's memories than a large museum with full visitor services.</p><p>However, no official announcement has been found confirming opening hours, admission fees, the direct custodian, the building's latest condition, or a museum-specific restoration project in 2026 (B.E. 2569). Old-town and cultural-street activities continue at municipal and community levels, but this should not be interpreted as evidence that the museum opens every day.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <span class="source-offline">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce) <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span> · <a href="https://www.phangngapao.go.th/travel/detail/89" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Phang Nga Province: Takuapa Old Town</a> · <span class="source-offline">สถานีวิทยุกระจายเสียงแห่งประเทศไทย (Radio Thailand) <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1847 (2390 BE)</p><h3>Establishment of Wat Sena Nucharangsan</h3><p>Temple records state it was established in 1847 (2390 BE); local sources identify Phraya Senanuchit (Nuch) as the founder.</p><a href="https://www.50amfh.org/userfiles/file/News/Thai%20temple%20name%20list/south/Phangnga.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2026 (2569 BE)</p><h3>Part of old town tourism context</h3><p>Takua Pa Community Museum is mentioned as part of the old town cultural street, but no specific opening hours are announced.</p><span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Ordination hall registered as an ancient monument</h3><p>The Fine Arts Department registered the ordination hall, but the reviewed sources do not specify the year.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4412" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Community museum established in a two-story building</h3><p>Academic sources describe the building and exhibits, but the establishment year and founder are not found.</p><a href="https://so05.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/parichartjournal/article/download/219292/168797/871014" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Two-storey museum building</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The community museum is located within Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan.</p><a href="https://so05.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/parichartjournal/article/download/219292/168797/871014" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Mining-era tools and utensils</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>It houses items from the mining era and rare objects reflecting local life.</p><a href="https://so05.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/parichartjournal/article/download/219292/168797/871014" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Chinese-influenced ordination hall</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The large ordination hall features designs influenced by Chinese architecture.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4412" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa old town context</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Situated in an old town community featuring Sino-Portuguese buildings and mining heritage.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2026-03-01 · Radio Thailand</p><h3>Phang Nga hosts the 12th 'From Takola to Takua Pa' event</h3><p>The event promotes Takua Pa old town tourism, linking to local lifestyle learning and community economy, but the news does not directly confirm activities inside the museum.</p><span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2024-08-28 · Government Public Relations Department</p><h3>Tracing the legend of Takola to the charm of Takua Pa old town</h3><p>Phang Nga province and the municipality promote old town tourism and stimulate the community economy. No specific mention of museum restoration.</p><a href="https://www.prd.go.th/th/content/category/detail/id/2040/iid/319567" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan was formerly known as "Wat Mai Kamphaeng", and its ordination hall was influenced by Chinese architecture.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4412" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The Takua Pa Community Museum is a two-storey building that houses utensils from the tin-mining era.</p><a href="https://so05.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/parichartjournal/article/download/219292/168797/871014" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>Sin Chai Tung Shrine <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://mapcarta.com/N7619565714" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/kue-chai/">Kue Chai Tung Shrine</a> <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></li><li><a href="/en/places/khun-in/">Khun In House</a> <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></li><li><a href="/en/places/governor-wall/">Governor’s Residence Wall</a> <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>How to dress</summary><p>Modest attire is recommended when entering the temple grounds.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>Takuapa Community Museum is a two-storey building inside Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan. It collects household items and equipment reflecting life in Takuapa, including objects from the mining era. Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan was built by Phraya Sena Nuchit (Nuch), and its ordination hall shows Chinese architectural influence.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>The community museum is inside Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan. It preserves mining-era objects and rare items reflecting local life. The large ordination hall is influenced by Chinese architecture.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Cultural environments for conservation (ONEP)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4412" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">วารสารปาริชาต มหาวิทยาลัยทักษิณ (Parichart Journal, Thaksin University)</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://so05.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/parichartjournal/article/download/219292/168797/871014" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Community database, Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Mapcarta / OpenStreetMap</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mapcarta.com/N7619565714" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Phang Nga Province temple registration report</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.50amfh.org/userfiles/file/News/Thai%20temple%20name%20list/south/Phangnga.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Department of Archaeology, Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">MGR Online</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9610000016873" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Takua Pa Town</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สารสนเทศท้องถิ่นภาคใต้ฝั่งอันดามัน (Andaman Southern Thai Local Information)</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.andamannlttrang.com/%E0%B8%82%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B9%E0%B8%A5/%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B9%82%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%96%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%8A%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%A3/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><span class="source-offline">Open source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สถานีวิทยุกระจายเสียงแห่งประเทศไทย (Radio Thailand)</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><span class="source-offline">Open source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Direct opening hours for the museum could not be found.</li><li>Verified admission fees for the museum could not be found.</li><li>Direct phone numbers, Facebook pages, websites, or LINE accounts for the museum could not be found.</li><li>Distances and routes from Takua Pa town centre, Phuket, Khao Lak, or the airport could not be found.</li><li>Verified information on the establishment year, founder, and registration details of the museum building itself could not be found.</li><li>Verified information on parking, restrooms, or wheelchair accessibility could not be found.</li><li>A verified duration for visits could not be found.</li><li>Details regarding specific museum activities in 2026 CE have not been found.</li><li>Evidence confirming the museum was abandoned, changed hands, or directly affected by the 2004 CE tsunami has not been found.</li><li>Official image links with verified usage rights could not be found.</li><li>No direct custodian, opening hours, admission fees, or announcement confirming that it remains open to visitors in 2026 (B.E. 2569) has been found.</li><li>No news from the past five years mentioning restoration or a museum-specific project has been found.</li><li>No verified image URL has been found that can be clearly identified as showing the museum itself, so photos_archive and photos_current are left as empty arrays.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
