"url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/thung-phra/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/thung-phra.webp", "description": "เอกสารกล่าวถึงซากหม้อไอน้ำเรือกลไฟซึ่งโยงกับการค้าในอดีต", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "postalCode": "82110", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.8293, "longitude": 98.36792}}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "เดินทางจากตัวเมืองตะกั่วป่าอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "อยู่ในเขตเมืองตะกั่วป่า ใกล้วัดหน้าม่วงและกำแพงเมืองเก่า; ใช้แผนที่นำทางไปยังพิกัดที่ระบุ"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "สวนสาธารณะทุ่งพระโพธิ์อยู่ในพื้นที่เมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่าที่อยู่ภายใต้ขอบเขตการควบคุมการก่อสร้างตามเทศบัญญัติ เอกสารแผนงานของเทศบาลระบุว่าสวนแห่งนี้มีสวนสุขภาพและสนามเด็กเล่น"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "เอกสารเทศบาลระบุว่าพื้นที่สวนสาธารณะเทศบาล ซึ่งรวมทุ่งพระโพธิ์ มีสวนสุขภาพ เอกสารเทศบาลระบุว่าพื้นที่สวนสาธารณะเทศบาลมีสนามเด็กเล่น อยู่ใกล้กำแพงเมืองเก่าและวัดหน้าม่วงตามข้อมูลแผนที่"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/thung-phra/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/thung-phra/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/thung-phra/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/thung-phra/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Parks & Public Spaces</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place notes · Parks and public spaces</span><h1>Thung Phra Pho Park</h1><p class="english">Thung Phra Pho Park</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">5 verified items</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="thung-phra">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/thung-phra.webp" alt="สวนสาธารณะทุ่งพระโพธิ์" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8293, 98.36792 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8293,98.36792" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://mapcarta.com/W815944528" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>From a riverside field to a town park</h3><p class="era-years"></p><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p>Accessible documents have not yet specified the starting year of construction, the builder, or the first project of Thung Phra Pho Public Park. Therefore, the "origin of the park" can only be told as much as the evidence allows. The park should not be tied directly to the tin mining era or maritime trade because there are still no documents to verify such continuity.</p><p>The context of the area is Takua Pa town in the old town zone, which has a history of settlement and trade across various eras, including the Chinese community and the mining economy. However, the verified role of Thung Phra Pho in contemporary documents is a public open space for town activities, not a mining building or an archaeological site with clearly identified builder histories.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://clib.psu.ac.th/southerninfo/content/1/3571b08d" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Southern Thailand Local Database, Prince of Songkla University</a> · <a href="https://download.asa.or.th/03media/04law/cba/mb/mb56-png.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Royal Gazette, Takua Pa Old Town building control ordinance</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>A public space handling water, merit making, and town adaptation</h3><p class="era-years">2013 to 2022 (B.E. 2556 to 2565)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>In 2013 (2556 BE), the park was named in the building control announcement of the Takua Pa old town area, meaning this area is within the old town landscape where the state dictates construction control. However, the announcement did not state the year of construction or the original layout of the park.</p><p>Municipal plan documents during the 2022 (2565 BE) fiscal year specified a project to construct and install electrical control cabinets inside the park with a budget of 460,000 baht, and also specified a project to dredge the Thung Phra Pho irrigation canal and construct a Takua Pa canal pier (Thung Phra Pho). This reflects that the park is related to water management and town infrastructure. Meanwhile, a 2013 (2556 BE) news report recorded that Thung Phra Pho was an installation point for water pumps when flooding occurred.</p><p>Old town project documents specify holding Loy Krathong (November full moon festival) here on the full moon day of the 12th lunar month, along with krathong contests, performances, and folk games. As for the evidence found, it does not yet verify the impact of the 2004 (2547 BE) tsunami, abandonment, change of hands, or the registration of the park specifically as an archaeological site.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://download.asa.or.th/03media/04law/cba/mb/mb56-png.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Royal Gazette, Takua Pa Old Town building control ordinance</a> · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_strategy/2022-12_231dcd9d5169573.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) Operation Plan 2022 (2565 BE)</a> · <a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9560000096203" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MGR Online: Takua Pa flood news</a> · <a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สผ. (ONEP) Takua Pa Old Town boundary delineation project</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A municipal park that remains a stage for daily life</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Current map data identifies Thung Phra Pho as a public park in Tambon Talat Yai, near Wat Na Mueang, Fire Station 2, and the old city wall. Thus, it still serves as an open space in the old town area, but no official announcement has been found that verifies opening and closing hours, admission fees, or specific on-site facilities.</p><p>The verified usage in 2026 (2569 BE) is that Rongrian Takua Pa Khiri Khet (Takua Pa Khiri Khet School) organized a Takuapa Walk Rally activity on 8 March 2026 (2569 BE) at Thung Phra Pho Public Park and the old town area, reflecting the use of the park as an outdoor learning spot, promoting health, and publicizing local culture.</p><p>Municipal documents also verify the picture of usage for health and children, such as a health park and a playground, and old town documents specify Loy Krathong as an annual activity. However, the latest physical condition reports, long-term restoration projects, or more detailed caretaker announcements other than being a municipal area have not yet been found.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://mapcarta.com/W815944528" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mapcarta / OpenStreetMap</a> · <a href="https://www.keereekatschool.ac.th/gallery-detail_1497" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rongrian Takua Pa Khiri Khet (Takua Pa Khiri Khet School): Takuapa Walk Rally 2026 activity</a> · <a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สผ. (ONEP) Takua Pa Old Town boundary delineation project</a> · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Thetsaban Mueang Takua Pa (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Environmental plan documents</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2013 (2556 BE)</p><h3>Park within the old town building control zone</h3><p>The Royal Gazette lists the park as an exception within the construction control boundary of Takua Pa old town.</p><a href="https://download.asa.or.th/03media/04law/cba/mb/mb56-png.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2021 (2564 BE)</p><h3>Municipality manages electricity and water plans</h3><p>There are projects to install electrical control cabinets in the park and plans regarding the Thung Phra Pho canal or pier.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_strategy/2022-12_231dcd9d5169573.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">8 March 2026 (2569 BE)</p><h3>Checkpoint for the Old Town Walk Rally</h3><p>Takua Pa Khiri Khet School uses the park and the old town area as a route for cultural learning and health promotion activities.</p><a href="https://www.keereekatschool.ac.th/gallery-detail_1497" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Year of establishment not verified</h3><p>No documents directly stating the year, founders, or reasons for establishing the park have been verified.</p><a href="https://mapcarta.com/W815944528" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Health park</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Municipal documents state that the municipal park area, which includes Thung Phra Pho, has a health park.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Proximity to the Sunday Market</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Municipal documents state that the municipal park area has a playground.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Location in the old town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located near the old town wall and Wat Na Muang according to map data.</p><a href="https://mapcarta.com/W815944528" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2026-03-08 · Rongrian Takua Pa Khiri Khet (Takua Pa Khiri Khet School)</p><h3>Takua Pa Khiri Khet School participates in Takua Pa Walk Rally 2026 (2569 BE)</h3><p>The event uses Thung Phra Pho Public Park and the old town area as a walking and running route to learn about local history and culture.</p><a href="https://www.keereekatschool.ac.th/gallery-detail_1497" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Thung Phra Pho is the venue for the Loy Krathong festival in Takua Pa old town on the full moon day of the 12th lunar month, featuring contests and performances.</p><a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The municipal plan included a project to install an electrical control cabinet in the park with a budget of 460,000 baht.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_strategy/2022-12_231dcd9d5169573.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located in Takua Pa town, near Wat Na Muang and the old town wall; use navigation maps to reach the specified coordinates.</p><a href="https://mapcarta.com/W815944528" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No readable sources found specifying the route and specific distance to this park</p><a href="https://mapcarta.com/W815944528" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No readable sources found specifying the route and specific distance to this park</p><a href="https://mapcarta.com/W815944528" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No readable sources found specifying the route and specific distance to this park</p><a href="https://mapcarta.com/W815944528" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>Wat Na Muang <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://mapcarta.com/W815944528" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li>Old Town Wall <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://mapcarta.com/W815944528" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li>Bung Tao Kong Shrine <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://mapcarta.com/W815944528" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/phra-narai/">Phra Narai Park</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Located in Takua Pa town, near Wat Na Muang and the old town wall; use navigation maps to reach the specified coordinates.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>Thung Phra Pho Public Park is in the Takua Pa old town area under the construction control boundaries according to municipal ordinances. Municipal plan documents state that this park has a health park and a playground.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>Municipal documents state that the municipal public park area, including Thung Phra Pho, has a health park. Municipal documents state that the municipal public park area has a playground. It is near the old city wall and Wat Na Mueang according to map data.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Mapcarta / OpenStreetMap</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mapcarta.com/W815944528" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Royal Gazette, Takua Pa Old Town building control ordinance</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://download.asa.or.th/03media/04law/cba/mb/mb56-png.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) Environmental Operation Plan</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Samnakngan Noyobai Lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat Lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning): Old town area boundary determination project</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Witthayalai Kan Achip Takua Pa (Takua Pa Industrial and Community Education College)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://tapc.ac.th/news-detail_137_2191" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">MGR Online</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9560000124259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) Operation Plan 2022 (2565 BE)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_strategy/2022-12_231dcd9d5169573.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สผ. (ONEP) Takua Pa Old Town boundary delineation project</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Rongrian Takua Pa Khiri Khet (Takua Pa Khiri Khet School)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.keereekatschool.ac.th/gallery-detail_1497" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">MGR Online</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9560000096203" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Opening hours: No official announcement found.</li><li>Admission fee: No data found.</li><li>Phone number, Facebook page, website, and LINE specific to the park: Not found.</li><li>Address and verified postal code for the specific point: No primary source found.</li><li>Founding year and creator: Not found.</li><li>The steamboat boiler and its trade connection: Found only in initial user data, so it is not cited as evidence.</li><li>Details on wheelchair access, parking, restrooms, and best time to visit: Not found.</li><li>A verified duration for visits could not be found.</li><li>The founding year, creator, and reason for establishing the park.</li><li>Specific role during the tin mining era, maritime trade, and town governor era.</li><li>Impact from the 2004 tsunami.</li><li>Abandonment, change of hands, or other uses in the past.</li><li>Registration as a historical site specifically for the park.</li><li>Opening hours, admission fee, latest physical condition, parking, restrooms, and wheelchair access.</li><li>Restoration or development projects ongoing in 2026.</li><li>Old and current photos with verifiable usage rights.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
site\en\places\wat-khuha\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Wat Khuha Phimuk · Wat Khuan Tham Phang Nga · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="Small details that invite you to pause and look · Wat Khuha Phimuk Takua Pa · smallest ubosot in Thailand · Takua Pa temple"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Wat Khuha Phimuk · Wat Khuan Tham Phang Nga"><meta property="og:description" content="Small details that invite you to pause and look · Wat Khuha Phimuk Takua Pa · smallest ubosot in Thailand · Takua Pa temple"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-khuha/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/wat-khuha.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/wat-khuha.png"><meta name="generator" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/wat-khuha/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "หน้าแรก", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "วัดคุหาภิมุข (วัดควนถ้ำ) ตะกั่วป่า", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-khuha/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "TouristAttraction", "name": "วัดคุหาภิมุข (วัดควนถ้ำ)", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-khuha/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/wat-khuha.webp", "description": "เอกสารกล่าวถึงอุโบสถขนาดเล็กและลักษณะสถาปัตยกรรม", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.831526975, "longitude": 98.367913006}}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "อุโบสถของวัดสร้างขึ้นเมื่อ พ.ศ. 2513 โดยนางฮวดบี ฐานข้อมูล สผ. จัดวัดแห่งนี้อยู่ในประเภทวัด วัดร้าง ศาสนสถาน และระบุว่าอุโบสถมีขนาดเล็กที่สุดในประเทศไทย"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ฐานข้อมูล สผ. ระบุว่าเป็นอุโบสถที่มีขนาดเล็กที่สุดในประเทศไทย ภายในอุโบสถมีพระพุทธรูปหินแกะสลักเป็นภาพนูนต่ำ ด้านหลังอุโบสถมีอักขระจารึก"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "เอกสารเทศบาลกล่าวถึงที่นี่อย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "เอกสารกล่าวถึงอุโบสถขนาดเล็กและลักษณะสถาปัตยกรรม"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-khuha/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/wat-khuha/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-khuha/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/wat-khuha/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Temples & Pagodas</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place record · Temples and pagodas</span><h1>Wat Khuha Phimuk (the cave hill temple)</h1><p class="english">Wat Khuha Phimuk</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified 4 items</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="wat-khuha">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/wat-khuha.webp" alt="วัดคุหาภิมุข (วัดควนถ้ำ)" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.831526975, 98.367913006 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.831526975,98.367913006" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4415" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4415" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>A small ordination hall on Khuan Tham in the mining era of Takua Pa</h3><p class="era-years">1970 (2513 BE)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The clearest evidence specifying a construction year at this time is for the temple's small ordination hall, built in 1970 (2513 BE) by Mrs. Huatbi. As for the year the entire temple complex began construction and the reason for choosing the site, there are no confirming documents yet. Therefore, one should not recount history beyond the available evidence.</p><p>This temple emerged during the late era when Takua Pa still had shared memories with tin mining. The town has roots as a port community with trade exchanges among people of many nationalities. Later, the tin mining economy and the Chinese community played a significant role. However, no evidence has yet been found that the builders of the ordination hall or Wat Khuan Tham were directly connected to the governor, the mines, or the Hokkien Chinese group.</p><p>What can be seen of the site's role is its function as a community religious site, with the ordination hall serving as a center for rituals and local art. Inside is a bas-relief stone Buddha image, behind it is a character inscription, and the boundary markers (sema) around the ordination hall are shaped as Buddha images in various postures.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4415" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Samnakngan Noyobai lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning) · Conserved Cultural Environment Sites</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning) · History of Takua Pa</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>From a religious site to a deserted temple list: A transition with gaps</h3><p class="era-years">After 1970 (B.E. 2513) to before 2026 (B.E. 2569) (no year found for individual events)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Official data from the Samnakngan Nayobai Lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat Lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning) classifies Wat Khuha Phimuk (Wat Khuan Tham) in the 'temple, abandoned temple, religious site' category. Meanwhile, the central religious property register of the Samnakngan Phraphutthasatsana Haeng Chat (National Office of Buddhism) lists 'Wat Khuan Tham (abandoned)' in Takua Pa district. Thus, it can only be confirmed that the temple is recorded as abandoned in government databases; it is unknown when it became abandoned or for what reason.</p><p>Takua Pa town itself transitioned from a port and mining town. As tin mining operations gradually ceased, economic liveliness decreased, and the old town shifted to being valued as a community heritage. This context helps explain the backdrop of the town's transition, but there is still no direct evidence linking Wat Khuan Tham to the impact of the mine closures.</p><p>No evidence has been found verifying any specific year of restoration, change of ownership, other uses, the 2004 (B.E. 2547) tsunami event, or a specific historical site registration announcement by Krom Sinlapakon (Fine Arts Department) for this temple.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://onab.go.th/th/file/get/file/2021111871cc998239d7c8b8d77aa76b771a377b151224.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานพระพุทธศาสนาแห่งชาติ (National Office of Buddhism) · National central ecclesiastical property and deserted temples registration data</a> · <a href="https://elibrary.tsri.or.th/fullP/RDG60T0046/RDG60T0046V04/RDG60T0046V04_full.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sthaban Phiphitthaphan Kanrianru Haeng Chat (National Discovery Museum Institute) / Takua Pa Old Town Information Source</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning) · History of Takua Pa</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>Present day: An art site with a tiny ordination hall, but its operational status is unclear</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>In 2026 (B.E. 2569), discovered official sources still record this place as an "abandoned temple" and do not provide opening hours, admission fees, caretakers, or contact channels. Therefore, it cannot be verified whether the temple is open to visitors or if monks reside there.</p><p>A verified highlight is the very small ordination hall, which ONEP identifies as the smallest in Thailand. Inside, there is a low-relief carved stone Buddha image with an inscription on the back, and an ancient hermit statue in the front.</p><p>No news or public announcements have been found verifying restoration projects, developments, traditional activities, or community use of the area over the past 5 years. Therefore, the current condition of the building and regular activities should be checked with locals or area caretakers before being published as travel information.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4415" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Samnakngan Noyobai lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning) · Conserved Cultural Environment Sites</a> · <a href="https://onab.go.th/th/file/get/file/2021111871cc998239d7c8b8d77aa76b771a377b151224.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานพระพุทธศาสนาแห่งชาติ (National Office of Buddhism) · National central ecclesiastical property and deserted temples registration data</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1970 (B.E. 2513)</p><h3>Construction of the Small Ordination Hall</h3><p>The ordination hall was built by Mrs. Huatbi, featuring a carved stone Buddha image, an inscription, and boundary stones (sema) shaped like Buddha images.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4415" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Temple Recorded as Abandoned</h3><p>The ONEP database and the National Office of Buddhism's registry list Wat Khuan Tham as an abandoned temple, though the year it was abandoned is not verified.</p><a href="https://onab.go.th/th/file/get/file/2021111871cc998239d7c8b8d77aa76b771a377b151224.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>No Evidence of Historical Site Registration Found</h3><p>This search did not find a Fine Arts Department registration announcement specifically confirming Wat Khuha Phimuk in Takua Pa.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4415" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Small ordination hall</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The ONEP database identifies it as the smallest ordination hall in Thailand.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4415" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Carved stone Buddha</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Inside the ordination hall is a low-relief carved stone Buddha.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4415" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Inscription behind the ordination hall</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>There are inscribed characters behind the ordination hall.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4415" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Buddha-shaped boundary markers</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The boundary markers around the hall are shaped like Buddha images in various postures.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4415" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Ancient hermit statue</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>An ancient hermit statue stands at the front of the temple.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4415" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>ONEP notes that the ordination hall of Wat Khuha Phimuk is the smallest in Thailand.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4415" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>There is an inscription behind the ordination hall, and the boundary markers around it are shaped like Buddha images in various postures.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4415" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li><a href="/en/places/wat-boromthat/">Wat Boromthat Khiri Khet (the town's relic temple)</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-pathum/">Wat Pathum Thara (the front town temple)</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-kongkha/">Wat Kongkha Phimuk (the riverside temple)</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-nikorn/">Wat Nikornwararam</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-sena/">Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>The temple's ordination hall was built in 1970 (B.E. 2513) by Mrs. Huat Bi. The ONEP database categorises this temple as a temple, an abandoned temple, and a religious site, stating that the ordination hall is the smallest in Thailand.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>The ONEP database states that it is the smallest ordination hall in Thailand. Inside the ordination hall, there is a low-relief carved stone Buddha image. Behind the ordination hall, there are inscribed characters.</p></details><details><summary>How the municipality document mentions this place</summary><p>Documents mention the small ordination hall and its architectural characteristics.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning) (ONEP) · Conserved Cultural Art Sites</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4415" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานพระพุทธศาสนาแห่งชาติ (National Office of Buddhism) · National central ecclesiastical property and deserted temples registration data</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://onab.go.th/th/file/get/file/2021111871cc998239d7c8b8d77aa76b771a377b151224.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Samnakngan Noyobai lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning) · Conserved Cultural Environment Sites</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4415" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning) · History of Takua Pa</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Takua Pa Old Town Community Research Report</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://elibrary.tsri.or.th/fullP/RDG60T0046/RDG60T0046V04/RDG60T0046V04_full.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>House numbers, streets, and postal codes are not verified from accessible sources.</li><li>Opening hours, admission fees, and recommended visit durations are not verified.</li><li>Phone numbers, Facebook pages, websites, or LINE accounts of the temple are not verified.</li><li>Verified travel methods and distances from Takua Pa town, Phuket, Khao Lak, or the airport are not verified.</li><li>Parking, restrooms, and accessibility for the elderly/wheelchairs are not verified.</li><li>Festivals or traditions linked to the temple from accessible sources are not verified.</li><li>Nearby places confirmed to be within walking distance are not verified.</li><li>Official image links for the location are not verified.</li><li>Official or academic sources confirming its role in the tin mining era, Sino-Portuguese/Chinese architecture, or historical site registration are not verified.</li><li>The founding year, founder, reasons for construction, and specific roles during the era of town rulers/tin mines/maritime trade are not verified.</li><li>The year it became deserted, the cause of abandonment, ownership changes, or other uses are not verified.</li><li>Specific evidence for the temple regarding the impact of the 2004 tsunami is not verified.</li><li>Years and details of renovations are not verified.</li><li>Announcements confirming historical site registration by the Fine Arts Department are not verified.</li><li>Current caretakers, opening hours, admission fees, community activities, and development projects in 2026 are not verified.</li><li>News from the past 5 years directly related to this temple is not verified.</li><li>URLs of old or current photos confirmed to be Wat Khuha Phimuk in Takua Pa are not verified. Do not mix photos of Wat Khuha Phimuk in Yala or Wat Kongkha Phimuk in Takua Pa.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
site\en\places\culture-street\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="Reading windows, shop signs, and life on the street · Takua Pa Culture Street · Takua Pa Old Town walking street · Takua Pa Sunday market"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street"><meta property="og:description" content="Reading windows, shop signs, and life on the street · Takua Pa Culture Street · Takua Pa Old Town walking street · Takua Pa Sunday market"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/places/culture-street/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/culture-street.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/culture-street.png"><meta name="generator" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/culture-street/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "หน้าแรก", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/places/culture-street/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "TouristAttraction", "name": "ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/culture-street/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/culture-street.webp", "description": "ย่านถนนคนเดินที่เชื่อมอาคารเก่า อาหาร และวิถีท้องถิ่น", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "ถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า และถนนอุดมธารา", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.829848, "longitude": 98.364073}, "telephone": "076424279"}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "เปิดให้เข้าชมเวลาใด", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "วันอาทิตย์ 14.00 ถึง 20.00 น."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีค่าเข้าชมหรือไม่", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ข้อมูลยังไม่ยืนยัน · เข้าชมฟรี"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "เดินทางจากตัวเมืองตะกั่วป่าอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ใช้ถนนราษฎร์บำรุงเข้าสู่ย่านเมืองเก่า แล้วต่อถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า; ช่วงถนนคนเดินอยู่บริเวณถนนศรีตะกั่วป่าและอุดมธารา"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "อาคารในย่านเมืองเก่ารักษาร่องรอยสถาปัตยกรรมชิโน-โปรตุกีส/ชิโน-ตะกั่วป่าที่สัมพันธ์กับยุคเหมืองแร่ดีบุก"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "อาคารบ้านเรือนและตึกแถวชิโน-โปรตุกีสในย่านเมืองเก่า อาหารพื้นเมือง ขนมพื้นบ้าน และของกินท้องถิ่น การแสดงศิลปวัฒนธรรม การละเล่นพื้นเมือง และการแต่งกายแบบบาบ๋า"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/culture-street/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/culture-street/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/culture-street/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/culture-street/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Markets & Food</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Saved places · Markets and food</span><h1>Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street</h1><p class="english">Takua Pa Culture Street</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">6 items verified</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="culture-street">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/shophouse-305.webp" width="400" height="300" alt="ตึกแถวเลขที่ 305 บนถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า" loading="eager"><figcaption>Shophouse number 305 on the old town culture street<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.829848, 98.364073 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.829848,98.364073" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><span class="source-offline">Coordinates source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd>Sundays, 2:00 PM to 8:00 PM <span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd>Free admission <span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd>076424279 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><span class="source-offline">Visitor information sources ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><span class="source-offline">Contact information ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#gallery">Gallery</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#nearby-note"></a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>From a mining town commercial street to a stage for past stories</h3><p class="era-years">1827 to 2007 (B.E. 2370 to 2550)</p><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p>This street was not originally created as a tourist attraction. It grew within Takua Pa old town, a port and water-trade center that later prospered during the tin-mining era. Chinese people from mainland China, Penang, and Singapore came to trade and mine, and shophouses, shops, hotels, coffee shops, and service businesses lined Thanon Udom Thara and Thanon Si Takua Pa.</p><p>The buildings on both sides of the street are therefore evidence of a multicultural town, including Chinese-style shophouses and colonial-influenced buildings linked to the Baba community. The street served as the town's commercial and residential spine, not as the pedestrian street it is today.</p><p>When the walking-street project began in 2007 (B.E. 2550), through cooperation among the Tourism Authority of Thailand (TAT), Phang Nga Office, Takua Pa Town Municipality, Talat Yai Community, and Senanuch Rangsan Community, the original street was turned into a public space for telling its history and reviving the community economy under the name “Takua Pa Old Town: Telling the Past”.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://anyflip.com/yxwin/sydm/basic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">A Hundred Stories of Andaman Old Towns / Academic documents on Takua Pa old town</a> · <a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9650000044214" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Manager Online: Experiencing the atmosphere of the cultural street</a> · <a href="https://so04.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/yru_human/article/download/128497/96582/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Yala Rajabhat University Journal</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>The mining town slowed down, but the old street did not disappear</h3><p class="era-years">1957 to 2022 (B.E. 2500 to 2565)</p><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p>After mining companies closed and tin production declined, the economy of Takua Pa's old commercial district stagnated. Some buildings remained in good condition, while others deteriorated over time. Area studies indicate that the cultural street uses stories, food, local knowledge, and existing architecture as assets to bring people and income back to the district.</p><p>The project name later changed from “Takua Pa Old Town: Telling the Past” to “Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street”. The Department of Internal Trade's market registry gives 17 December 2017 (B.E. 2560) as the establishment/promotional date, while news sources place the start of activities in 2007 (B.E. 2550). These should therefore be understood as separate milestones: the start of activities and the market's registration/promotion.</p><p>In 2022 (B.E. 2565), the province and local authorities were still holding green-season activities and offering free rides on pho thong trucks. This shows that the street was being used to distribute income and draw people back to the old district. No specific evidence was found that the entire street was damaged by the 2004 tsunami or that the entire street was registered as an ancient monument.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <span class="source-offline">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce) <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span> · <a href="https://mgronline.com/travel/detail/9650000061422" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Manager Online: Opening the street during the rainy season, 2022 (B.E. 2565)</a> · <a href="https://so04.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/JSTD/article/view/254126" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Research on cultural tourism in Takua Pa</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A Sunday market that keeps the old town alive</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The Department of Internal Trade's market registration records state that Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street is on Thanon Si Takua Pa and Thanon Udom Thara. It opens on Sundays from 14:00 to 20:00, with free entry to the activities. The records identify an operator at the market-system level but do not identify a separate legal entity responsible for the street.</p><p>Today, the street still serves as a market and community learning space, with local food and sweets, basketry, handicrafts, performances, Baba dress, photo exhibitions, and street art. The old Sino-Portuguese buildings remain the main setting for activities. Some are well preserved, while others show signs of deterioration over time. No announcement of a major restoration project specifically for this street was found in the sources checked.</p><p>Archived news confirms that events continued at least in 2022 (B.E. 2565), with community activities on the street in 2024 (B.E. 2567). It can therefore be concluded that the street is still used as a cultural market and activity space for local people. Actual opening hours may change by season or according to the organizer's announcements.</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/shophouse-305.webp" width="400" height="300" alt="ตึกแถวเลขที่ 305 บนถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Shophouse number 305 on the old town culture street<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">References · <span class="source-offline">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce) <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span> · <a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9670000097253" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Manager Online: The 9-baht merit-making vegetarian event, 2024 (B.E. 2567)</a> · <a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9650000044214" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Manager Online: The cultural street and street art</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1827 (B.E. 2370)</p><h3>Initial development of the town and Udomthara Road area</h3><p>Old town documents classify the period from 1827 to 1897 as the town's establishment and early development phase, with Udomthara Road being one of the first settlement areas.</p><a href="https://anyflip.com/yxwin/sydm/basic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1887 (B.E. 2430)</p><h3>Shophouses influenced by Penang and Singapore ports</h3><p>Sri Takua Pa Road features Straits Settlements colonial-influenced shophouses, which are linked to trade and the Chinese community in the port cities.</p><a href="https://anyflip.com/yxwin/sydm/basic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1957 (B.E. 2500)</p><h3>Takua Pa reached the peak of the mining era</h3><p>Documents explain that the town's prosperity peaked around 1957 before the mines closed and the commercial district stagnated.</p><a href="https://anyflip.com/yxwin/sydm/basic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p class="era-years">2007 (2550)</p><h3>Cultural walking street project began</h3><p>The TAT Phang Nga Office, Takua Pa Town Municipality, and the community started 'Takua Pa Old Town, Telling the Past'.</p><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9650000044214" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p class="era-years">17 December 2017 (B.E. 2560)</p><h3>Registered and promoted as a market</h3><p>The Department of Internal Trade's registry lists 17 December 2017 as the date of the market's establishment and promotion.</p><span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">26 June to 28 August 2022 (B.E. 2565)</p><h3>Street opened during the green season with free Pho Thong buses</h3><p>The province and local partners expanded Sunday activities to stimulate off-season tourism and distribute income.</p><a href="https://mgronline.com/travel/detail/9650000061422" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">10 October 2024 (B.E. 2567)</p><h3>Merit-making and 9-Baht vegetarian food event</h3><p>The street serves as a venue for vegetarian food activities and carrying on old town community traditions, with over 200 participating shops according to news reports.</p><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9670000097253" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><section class="research-section" id="gallery"><h2>Gallery</h2><div data-gallery><div class="gallery-tabs" hidden><button type="button" data-tab="today">Present photos</button><button type="button" data-tab="archive">Historical photos</button></div><div id="gallery-today" data-panel="today"><h3>Present photos</h3><div class="photo-grid"><figure class="research-photo"><a data-lightbox href="/assets/photos/shophouse-305.webp" aria-label="ขยายภาพ · ตึกแถวเลขที่ 305 บนถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า"><img src="/assets/photos/shophouse-305.webp" width="400" height="300" alt="ตึกแถวเลขที่ 305 บนถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Shophouse number 305 on the old town culture street<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></div><div id="gallery-archive" data-panel="archive"><h3>Historical photos</h3><div class="photo-grid"><p class="muted">No images authorized for publication in this category yet</p></div></div></div></section><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Old buildings</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Sino-Portuguese houses and shophouses in the old town district.</p><a href="https://travel.kapook.com/view275997.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Local food and snacks</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Native food, traditional sweets, and local eats.</p><span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Performances and community life</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Cultural performances, local folk games, and Baba dressing.</p><span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Street art</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Art and street art depicting local ways of life.</p><a href="https://travel.kapook.com/view275997.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2024-10-10 · Manager Online</p><h3>Merit-making and 9-Baht vegetarian food event in Takua Pa old town</h3><p>Vegetarian food activities and community traditions are held on the cultural street, with a large number of participants according to news reports.</p><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9670000097253" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2022-06-26 · Manager Online</p><h3>Phang Nga opens Takua Pa walking street in the rainy season with free Pho Thong buses</h3><p>Green season activities were held every Sunday from 26 June to 28 August 2022 to distribute income to the community.</p><a href="https://mgronline.com/travel/detail/9650000061422" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2022-04-17 · Department of Internal Trade</p><h3>Takua Pa old town cultural street in the Must-See Market activity</h3><p>The Department of Internal Trade reported on activities promoting community market channels at the Takua Pa old town cultural street.</p><span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p>The activity's original name was "Takua Pa Old Town, Telling Stories of the Past" before changing to Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street.</p><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9650000044214" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Many shophouses on Sri Takuapa Road have a covered front walkway called Ngo Kha Ki, which helps shield from sun and rain.</p><a href="https://anyflip.com/yxwin/sydm/basic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Use Rat Bamrung Road into the old town, then connect to Sri Takuapa Road. The walking street section is located around Sri Takuapa and Udomthara Roads.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li><a href="/en/places/governor-wall/">Governor’s Residence Wall</a> <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></li><li>Wat Na Mueang <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/riverwalk/">Takuapa Riverwalk</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/food-center/">Takua Pa Open-Air Food Center</a></li></ul></section><aside class="nearby-note"><span class="chapter">Stop nearby</span><p>Shophouse No. 53 on Thanon Rat Bamrung in the old market district is a teak house that now operates as a cafe, making it one of the few buildings on this street that visitors can enter and see inside.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://siwaracafe.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Siwara Cafe · A teak house on this street ↗</a></aside><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Opening hours</summary><p>Sundays, 2:00 PM to 8:00 PM</p></details><details><summary>Admission fee</summary><p>Not verified · Free admission</p></details><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Use Rat Bamrung Road into the old town, then connect to Sri Takuapa Road. The walking street section is located around Sri Takuapa and Udomthara Roads.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>Buildings in the old town area preserve traces of Sino-Portuguese or Sino-Takua Pa architecture related to the tin mining era.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>Homes and Sino-Portuguese shophouses in the old town, local food, traditional sweets and local snacks, cultural performances, traditional games, and Baba dress</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><span class="source-offline">Open source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Database of important archaeological sites in Thailand</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Kapook Travel</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://travel.kapook.com/view275997.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Naewna</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.naewna.com/local/537042" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><span class="source-offline">Open source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">A Hundred Stories of Andaman Old Towns</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://anyflip.com/yxwin/sydm/basic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Manager Online</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9650000044214" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Manager Online</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mgronline.com/travel/detail/9650000061422" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Research on developing Peranakan cultural tourism routes</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://so04.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/JSTD/article/view/254126" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Kapook Travel</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://travel.kapook.com/view275997.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Postal code for this street not found directly from read sources.</li><li>Verified data on parking, restrooms, wheelchair access, and visit duration not found.</li><li>Facebook page, website, or LINE verified from read sources not found.</li><li>Verified distance from Phuket, Khao Lak, or the airport not found.</li><li>Specific creators of the cultural street not found.</li><li>Evidence that the cultural street itself is registered as a historical site not found; the registration found is for the Takua Pa governor's residence wall.</li><li>Lunar calendar dates for the event not found.</li><li>Direct official image links with verifiable usage rights not found, so photos are omitted.</li><li>Direct evidence that this street was damaged by the 2004 tsunami not verified yet.</li><li>Historical site registration announcement specifying this entire street not found yet.</li><li>Documents specifying the individual founder or responsible person for the street in 2007 not found yet.</li><li>Official announcements for major restoration projects specifically for the street up to 2026 not found yet.</li><li>Old photos with clear usage rights for this street not found yet, so the photos_archive array is empty.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
