.\build_kuapapoh_story.py:63:        "มิติที่สามคือ “อาหาร” ที่เน้นย้ำถึงอาหารท้องถิ่น รสชาติดั้งเดิม และร้านอาหารจากยุคเหมืองแร่ที่สืบทอดสูตรต่อกันมาจนถึงปัจจุบัน ส่วน “อารมณ์” นำเสนอผลงานของศิลปินท้องถิ่น ทั้งภาพวาด การร้องรำทำเพลง ไปจนถึงเสียงกลองที่เร้าใจในช่วงเทศกาลกินผัก ซึ่งล้วนเป็นสิ่งที่ปลุกเร้าความรู้สึกของผู้มาเยือน",
.\build_part6.py:13:        "headline": "From port and mine traces to a municipal public space",
.\build_part6.py:81:        "body": "Currently, the residence wall area is open for viewing daily with no admission fee. The Fine Arts Department, Takua Pa Town Municipality, and the Na Nakhon family are listed as joint caretakers. The overall condition of the wall is stable, with a lawn and some walkways, but weeds and trees are found clinging to the wall, which is a maintenance issue warned about by the archaeological database.\n\nIn 2026 AD, the municipality organized the 12th 'From Takola to Takua Pa' event between 28 February and 3 March. The Takua Pa Governor Worship Ceremony was held on the morning of 3 March at the governor's residence, followed by a Buddhist chanting ceremony. The event also connected with cultural performances and the sale of local food, community products, and cultural street activities. This shows that the ceremony today serves to connect the town's memory with tourism economics and community participation. Announcements confirming the next ceremony schedule or new restoration projects for 2026 AD are not verified."
.\build_part6.py:167:        "body": "The latest found evidence confirms that the tradition is still held continuously. A 2024 AD public relations news report states that the Takua Pa old town event from 3 to 11 October included 29 participating shrines and vegetarian halls. Local government agencies and the Provincial Administrative Organization collaborated on public relations, while the shrines prepared the rituals.\n\nCurrently, the event space is not a single building but a ritual landscape of multiple shrines, Sri Takua Pa Road, and the Talat Yai area. Confirmed activities include raising the Go Teng pole, Buddha processions, spirit medium ceremonies, fire-walking, merit-making, and vegetarian food. The community uses the festival as a space to make merit, meet, and welcome tourists, with participants commonly dressing in white.\n\nConfirmed data on the physical condition of all shrines, opening hours, admission fees, specific tradition restoration projects, or a single central caretaker is not verified. Visitors should verify the schedule with the municipality and shrines again in the year of travel."
.\build_part6.py:230:        "headline": "From municipal plans to activities at multiple waterfront points",
.\build_part6.py:231:        "body": "The Takua Pa Town Municipality's action plan document lists the Loy Krathong tradition under religious, cultural, and recreational missions, alongside krathong-making contests, stage performances, and exhibitions or pier decorations. This picture reflects how the tradition is managed as a local public event, but the document does not state the starting year, founder, or any transfer of management.\n\nEvidence confirming that the activity was abandoned, restored, or registered as an archaeological site is not verified, because Loy Krathong is a tradition and event locations can change; it is not a building with a unified registration. Furthermore, news or reports specific to Takua Pa explaining how the 2004 AD tsunami affected the event or the canal are not verified.\n\nEvidence from 2025 AD indicates activities were held at Takua Pa Canal in Takua Pa subdistrict and Bang Muang Canal in Bang Muang subdistrict, with many people attending. A significant development is seen from an event planned by the municipality to activities utilizing waterfront spaces at more than one point depending on the year's context."
