alt="กำแพงจวนเจ้าเมืองตะกั่วป่า" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">17</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Old Buildings & City Traces</span><h3><a href="/en/places/governor-wall/">Governor’s Residence Wall</a></h3><p>A trace on the wall that tells the town's story</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="heritage" data-name="บ้านขุนอินทร์"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/khun-in/"><img src="/assets/khun-in.webp" alt="บ้านขุนอินทร์" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">18</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Old Buildings & City Traces</span><h3><a href="/en/places/khun-in/">Khun In House</a></h3><p>Windows and balconies inviting a look into the past</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="heritage" data-name="โรงเรียนเต้าหมิง"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/tao-ming/"><img src="/assets/tao-ming.webp" alt="โรงเรียนเต้าหมิง" width="1000" height="667" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">19</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Old Buildings & City Traces</span><h3><a href="/en/places/tao-ming/">Tao Ming School</a></h3><p>A building that passes on language and culture</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="park" data-name="สวนสาธารณะพระนารายณ์"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/phra-narai/"><img src="/assets/phra-narai.webp" alt="สวนสาธารณะพระนารายณ์" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">12</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Parks & Public Spaces</span><h3><a href="/en/places/phra-narai/">Phra Narai Park</a></h3><p>Rest area with stories of belief</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="park" data-name="สวนสาธารณะทุ่งพระโพธิ์"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/thung-phra/"><img src="/assets/thung-phra.webp" alt="สวนสาธารณะทุ่งพระโพธิ์" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">13</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Parks & Public Spaces</span><h3><a href="/en/places/thung-phra/">Thung Phra Pho Park</a></h3><p>Steamboat traces in the garden</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="market" data-name="ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/riverwalk/"><img src="/assets/riverwalk.webp" alt="ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">14</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Markets & Food</span><h3><a href="/en/places/riverwalk/">Takuapa Riverwalk</a></h3><p>Food and life by the river</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="market" data-name="ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/culture-street/"><img src="/assets/culture-street.webp" alt="ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">15</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Markets & Food</span><h3><a href="/en/places/culture-street/">Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street</a></h3><p>Walking and reading the city through buildings and people</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="market" data-name="ศูนย์อาหารลานโล่งตะกั่วป่า"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/food-center/"><img src="/assets/food-center.webp" alt="ศูนย์อาหารลานโล่งตะกั่วป่า" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">20</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Markets & Food</span><h3><a href="/en/places/food-center/">Takua Pa Open-Air Food Center</a></h3><p>Many flavors in one destination</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="museum" data-name="พิพิธภัณฑ์เสนานุชรังสรรค์ชุมชนตะกั่วป่า"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/museum/"><img src="/assets/museum.webp" alt="พิพิธภัณฑ์เสนานุชรังสรรค์ชุมชนตะกั่วป่า" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">07</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Museums</span><h3><a href="/en/places/museum/">Takua Pa Community Museum</a></h3><p>Preserving the town's stories together</p></div></article></div><div class="empty-state" data-place-empty hidden><h3>Haven't found this destination yet</h3><p>Try another search term or view all places</p><button type="button" data-clear-places>Clear filters</button></div></div><aside class="source"><h2>Data Sources</h2><p>Compiled from<a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takua Pa Town Municipality brochure</a> · Data extracted September 6, 2026 (2569 BE). The document does not specify a publication date. Opening hours, shop status, and current schedules are not verified. Please check with the venue before traveling.</p></aside></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
.\audit\a2-enq.log:221:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Tao Ming School · Takuapa old town · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="A school building that tells a story of cultural transmission · Tao Ming School Takuapa · Chinese school Takuapa · Sino-Portuguese Takuapa"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Tao Ming School · Takuapa old town"><meta property="og:description" content="A school building that tells a story of cultural transmission · Tao Ming School Takuapa · Chinese school Takuapa · Sino-Portuguese Takuapa"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/places/tao-ming/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/tao-ming.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/tao-ming.png"><meta name="generator" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/tao-ming/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "หน้าแรก", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "โรงเรียนเต้าหมิง · อาคารเต้าหมิง ตะกั่วป่า", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/places/tao-ming/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "TouristAttraction", "name": "โรงเรียนเต้าหมิง", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/tao-ming/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/tao-ming.webp", "description": "เกิดจากความร่วมมือของชาวจีนในตะกั่วป่าเพื่อการเรียนภาษาและวัฒนธรรมจีน", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "ถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า (ไม่พบเลขที่อาคารจากแหล่งที่อ่านได้)", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.8338139717, "longitude": 98.3649490347}}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "เดินทางจากตัวเมืองตะกั่วป่าอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "อยู่ในเขตชุมชนเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า บริเวณถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า; ใช้แผนที่นำทางไปยังพิกัดที่ระบุ"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "อาคารสร้างขึ้นใน พ.ศ. 2465 โรงเรียนเริ่มขอตั้งเป็นโรงเรียนราษฎร์ใน พ.ศ. 2463 และเดิมใช้ชื่อโต๊ะเบ๋ง ตามสำเนียงฮกเกี้ยน"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "อาคารโรงเรียนประวัติศาสตร์ที่ยังคงเหลืออยู่ในย่านเมืองเก่า สังเกตรูปทรงอาคารและหลังคามุงสังกะสีซึ่งระบุโดยหน่วยงานอนุรักษ์ เป็นหลักฐานของการจัดการศึกษาโดยชุมชนชาวจีนในเมืองเหมืองแร่ตะกั่วป่า"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/tao-ming/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/tao-ming/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/tao-ming/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/tao-ming/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Old Buildings & City Traces</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place record · Old buildings and city traces</span><h1>Tao Ming School</h1><p class="english">Tao Ming School</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">10 verified points</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="tao-ming">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/tao-ming-school.jpg" alt="อาคารโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า" loading="eager"><figcaption>Tao Ming School seen from the front, on the old town culture street<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8338139717, 98.3649490347 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8338139717,98.3649490347" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#gallery">Gallery</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>From mining town donations to Takua Pa's first Chinese school</h3><p class="era-years">1920 to 1922 (B.E. 2463 to 2465)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Before it had a permanent building, Tao Ming School informally taught Chinese through private instruction. When the Private Schools Act of 1918 (พ.ศ. 2461) came into effect, the school formally declared its intention to be established in 1920 (พ.ศ. 2463), using the name “To Beng” in Hokkien pronunciation, before changing to “Tao Ming” in Mandarin pronunciation. The name conveys the idea of leading toward knowledge.</p><p>The surviving building was constructed in 1922 (พ.ศ. 2465) with funds collected from mining magnates and Chinese merchants in the old market at Yan Yao, as well as merchant networks from Ranong and Phuket. Another official source describes it as the work of a Chinese merchants' association that entered the tin-mining industry to provide Chinese-language education for Chinese children. The adapted Sino-Portuguese building with its corrugated-metal roof was therefore not only a school, but evidence that wealth from mining, trade, and Chinese networks was becoming a community institution.</p><p>At that time, Takua Pa was a trading and transport district connected to the river and sea. The town grew through tin, while Chinese people from Hokkien, Guangdong, and Hainan came as workers, merchants, and entrepreneurs. The school helped give the Chinese community in the flourishing mining town a linguistic and cultural foundation.</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/tao-ming-logo.jpg" alt="ตราโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง" loading="lazy"><figcaption>The Tao Ming School emblem<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Samnakngan Noyobai lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning): Rongrian Tao Ming (Tao Ming School) building</a> · <a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Muang Boran Journal: Takua Pa Old Town and its endless tales</a> · <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Takua Pa Town</a> · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Environmental Operation Plan</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>When the mining town quieted down, the school paused, but the building still speaks</h3><p class="era-years">1977 to 2025 (B.E. 2520 to 2568)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Local sources state that Takua Pa's mines gradually closed from the 1970s, reducing the town's activity, while Tao Ming School ceased operations later. Verifiable official sources confirm only that “the school has been discontinued” and that the building is under the care of the Tao Ming School Foundation, Takua Pa. They do not specify the year it ceased operating or details of any change in ownership.</p><p>No readable evidence has been found confirming that the building was directly affected by the 2004 tsunami (พ.ศ. 2547) or that it underwent restoration in any particular year. It should therefore not be concluded that it was damaged or repaired because of that event, even though the Takua Pa area has sites connected with tsunami survivor assistance and the old town has regained a cultural-tourism role.</p><p>The old town boundary document by ONEP indicates the boundary passing through Tao Ming School, and the community database of the Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre classifies the building among the important evidence of the old town. However, this search has not yet found a Fine Arts Department announcement directly registering the “Tao Ming School Building”. Therefore, the conservation status of the area is separated from the registration status of the building.</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/tao-ming-logo.jpg" alt="ตราโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง" loading="lazy"><figcaption>The Tao Ming School emblem<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Muang Boran Journal: Takua Pa Old Town and its endless tales</a> · <a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning (ONEP): Takua Pa Old Town Boundary</a> · <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Takua Pa Town</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Samnakngan Noyobai lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning): Rongrian Tao Ming (Tao Ming School) building</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>The original building remains in the old town, but it is no longer an active school</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The currently verified status is that the school has closed down, leaving a historical building under the care of the Munlanithi Rongrian Tao Ming Takua Pa (Tao Ming Takua Pa School Foundation). Therefore, it should be understood that "visiting the building" is not the same as "visiting an operating school".</p><p>The building is located on Thanon Si Takua Pa in the old town area and is still used as a destination in tourism media by the Thetsaban Mueang Takua Pa (Takua Pa Town Municipality), the Kan Thongthiao Haeng Prathet Thai (Tourism Authority of Thailand), and old town activities, such as the cultural street held in the Thanon Si Takua Pa area. The information found verifies the context of activities in the area but it is not verified that activities are regularly held inside the building.</p><p>The condition verified from official sources is that the building remains and has architectural value in applied Sino-Portuguese style. As for opening hours, admission fees, regular caretakers, interior access, wheelchair accessibility, and the 2026 (2569 BE) restoration project, there is still no verifiable public information. Therefore, one should contact the caretaker or municipality before traveling.</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/tao-ming-school.jpg" alt="อาคารโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Tao Ming School seen from the front, on the old town culture street<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Samnakngan Noyobai lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning): Rongrian Tao Ming (Tao Ming School) building</a> · <a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1099396" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Tourism Authority of Thailand: TAT Media Assets · Tao Ming School</a> · <a href="https://www.phangngapao.go.th/travel/detail/89" target="_blank" rel="noopener">องค์การบริหารส่วนจังหวัดพังงา (Phang Nga Provincial Administrative Organization): Takua Pa Old Town</a> · <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qn0Tb1GSiZY" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Thetsaban Mueang Takua Pa (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Tao Ming School Building (location introduction video)</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1920 (2463 BE)</p><h3>Application for Toh Beng Private School</h3><p>The Chinese school, initially operated informally by private individuals, applied for private school status following the Private Schools Act of 1918.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1922 (2465 BE)</p><h3>Construction of Tao Ming School Building</h3><p>The applied Sino-Portuguese building was constructed with donations from tin mining tycoons and Chinese merchants to provide primary and Chinese language education for children in Takua Pa.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1977 to 1986 (2520s BE decade)</p><h3>Decline of the Mining Town</h3><p>Local sources state that tin mines began to gradually close during this decade, reducing the town's vibrancy. However, this is not a verified year for the school's closure.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2020 (2563 BE)</p><h3>Municipality Releases Promotional Video</h3><p>Takua Pa Municipality published a video introducing the Tao Ming School building as an old town tourist attraction.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qn0Tb1GSiZY" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">21 February 2026 (2569 BE)</p><h3>Old Town Storytelling Event at Tao Ming School</h3><p>Press releases indicated the Old Town Storytelling event took place at Tao Ming School, Takua Pa. However, full details from primary news sources are not verified.</p><a href="https://youphuket.club/author/admin/page/58/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>School Closes and Foundation Takes Over</h3><p>The exact year of closure is not verified. Official sources state the remaining building is under the care of the Tao Ming Takua Pa School Foundation.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><section class="research-section" id="gallery"><h2>Gallery</h2><div data-gallery><div class="gallery-tabs" hidden><button type="button" data-tab="today">Present photos</button><button type="button" data-tab="archive">Historical photos</button></div><div id="gallery-today" data-panel="today"><h3>Present photos</h3><div class="photo-grid"><figure class="research-photo"><a data-lightbox href="/assets/photos/tao-ming-school.jpg" aria-label="ขยายภาพ · อาคารโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า"><img src="/assets/photos/tao-ming-school.jpg" alt="อาคารโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Tao Ming School seen from the front, on the old town culture street<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></div><div id="gallery-archive" data-panel="archive"><h3>Historical photos</h3><div class="photo-grid"><figure class="research-photo"><a data-lightbox href="/assets/photos/tao-ming-logo.jpg" aria-label="ขยายภาพ · ตราโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง"><img src="/assets/photos/tao-ming-logo.jpg" alt="ตราโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>The Tao Ming School emblem<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></div></div></section><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Old yellow building</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>A historic school building that still remains in the old town area.</p><a href="https://readme.me/p/51787" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Applied Sino-Portuguese style</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Observe the building's shape and zinc roof, as noted by conservation agencies.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Traces of Chinese education</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>It is evidence of educational management by the Chinese community in the Takua Pa mining town.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2026-02-21 · YOUPHUKET</p><h3>Old Town Storytelling Event at Tao Ming School, Takua Pa</h3><p>Press releases reported a full day of activities hosted at Tao Ming School.</p><a href="https://youphuket.club/author/admin/page/58/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>"Toh Beng" is the original name pronounced in the Hokkien dialect, while "Tao Ming" is the Mandarin pronunciation of the name 導明.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p>Tao Ming School was the first and only Chinese language school in Takua Pa according to accessible local articles.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The building was constructed by Chinese craftsmen and features a zinc roof in the applied Sino-Portuguese style.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located in the Takua Pa old town community on Si Takua Pa Road; use a navigation map to the specified coordinates.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance was found from verified sources.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance was found from verified sources.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance was found from verified sources.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>Takua Pa Old Town Community / Talat Yai (Big Market) <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/iron-bridge/">Boon Soong Iron Bridge</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/governor-wall/">Governor’s Residence Wall</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/khun-in/">Khun In House</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Located in the Takua Pa old town community on Si Takua Pa Road; use a navigation map to the specified coordinates.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>The building was constructed in 1922 (2465 BE). The school started requesting to be established as a private school in 1920 (2463 BE) and originally used the name To Beng according to the Hokkien accent.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>A historical school building remaining in the old town area. Observe the building shape and corrugated zinc roof identified by conservation agencies. It is evidence of educational management by the Chinese community in the tin mining town of Takua Pa.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Samnakngan Noyobai lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning): Rongrian Tao Ming (Tao Ming School) building</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Takua Pa Town</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Muang Boran Journal: Takua Pa Old Town and its endless tales</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Readme.me: Hello Phang.Nga</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://readme.me/p/51787" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Environmental Operation Plan</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">องค์การบริหารส่วนจังหวัดพังงา (Phang Nga Provincial Administrative Organization): Takua Pa Old Town</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.phangngapao.go.th/travel/detail/89" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Tourism Authority of Thailand: TAT Media Assets · Tao Ming School</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1099396" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Thetsaban Mueang Takua Pa (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Tao Ming School Building</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qn0Tb1GSiZY" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">YOUPHUKET: Press release for the Old Town Tells Stories event</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://youphuket.club/author/admin/page/58/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>No building number or postal code found in accessible sources.</li><li>No official opening and closing hours found.</li><li>No admission fee found.</li><li>No official phone number, Facebook page, website, or LINE account found.</li><li>No verified information on parking, restrooms, and accessibility for wheelchairs or the elderly.</li><li>No information on registration as a historical site by the Fine Arts Department.</li><li>No information on individual builders found.</li><li>No festivals held directly at the school found.</li><li>Official image links with specified usage rights are not verified.</li><li>No year of school closure found, nor a list of administrators or teachers.</li><li>No verified evidence of ownership changes or use for other businesses after the school closed.</li><li>No verified evidence that the building was directly affected by the 2004 tsunami.</li><li>No year or documents confirming the specific restoration of the building found.</li><li>No Fine Arts Department announcement directly confirming the registration of the Tao Ming School building as a historical site.</li><li>No opening hours, admission fees, regular caretakers, interior access permissions, parking, restrooms, or wheelchair access found.</li><li>No verified restoration or development projects for the building in 2026 found.</li><li>No old photos with direct file URLs and clear usage rights found.</li><li>Activity news on February 21, 2026, was found on a PR aggregation page, but the main news or official announcement could not be fully read.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
.\audit\a2-enq.log:224:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Boon Soong Iron Bridge, Takua Pa · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="Looking at the steel frame and recalling the miners&#x27; journey · Khok Khanoon Iron Bridge · Takua Pa attractions · Phang Nga heritage"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Boon Soong Iron Bridge, Takua Pa"><meta property="og:description" content="Looking at the steel frame and recalling the miners&#x27; journey · Khok Khanoon Iron Bridge · Takua Pa attractions · Phang Nga heritage"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/places/iron-bridge/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/iron-bridge.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/iron-bridge.png"><meta name="generator" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/iron-bridge/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "หน้าแรก", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "สะพานเหล็กบุญสูง · สะพานเหล็กโคกขนุน", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/places/iron-bridge/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "TouristAttraction", "name": "สะพานเหล็กบุญสูง", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/iron-bridge/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/iron-bridge.webp", "description": "สะพานมีความเกี่ยวข้องกับการเดินทางและการขนส่งในยุคเหมืองแร่", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "ถนนราษฎร์บำรุง บ้านโคกขนุน", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "postalCode": "82110", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.8531719567, "longitude": 98.3540239936}}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "เปิดให้เข้าชมเวลาใด", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ข้อมูลยังไม่ยืนยัน · เข้าชมได้ตลอดทั้งวัน (ข้อมูลจากแหล่งท่องเที่ยวรอง)"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีที่จอดรถไหม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "มีข้อมูลจากรีวิวว่าจอดริมถนนได้และมีพื้นที่จำกัด แต่ไม่มีข้อมูลทางการยืนยัน"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "เดินทางจากตัวเมืองตะกั่วป่าอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "เดินทางตามถนนราษฎร์บำรุงไปทางเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า สะพานอยู่ด้านซ้ายมือ ห่างจากตัวเมืองประมาณ 2 กิโลเมตร"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "พ.ศ. 2511 มีการนำเหล็กจากเรือขุดแร่มาสร้างสะพานเหล็กโคกขนุน ความยาวกว่า 200 เมตร ข้ามแม่น้ำตะกั่วป่า ผู้ริเริ่มคือ นายจุติ บุญสูง เจ้าของกิจการบริษัทเรือขุดแร่จุติบุญสูง จำกัด ซึ่งก่อตั้งบริษัทใน พ.ศ. 2503"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "สะพานทอดข้ามแม่น้ำตะกั่วป่าและเชื่อมพื้นที่ถนนหลักกับบริเวณโรงขุดแร่เก่า ใช้เหล็กจากเรือขุดแร่ที่ไม่ใช้งานแล้ว และปลายทางยังมองเห็นโรงขุดแร่เก่า จากสะพานเห็นทุ่งสีเขียว ต้นไม้ และทิวเขา เหมาะกับการชมวิวและถ่ายภาพ"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/iron-bridge/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/iron-bridge/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/iron-bridge/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/iron-bridge/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Old Buildings & City Traces</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place record · Old buildings and city traces</span><h1>Boon Soong Iron Bridge</h1><p class="english">Boon Soong Iron Bridge</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">9 items verified</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="iron-bridge">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/iron-bridge.webp" alt="สะพานเหล็กบุญสูง" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8531719567, 98.3540239936 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8531719567,98.3540239936" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4421" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd>Open all day (information from secondary tourist sources) <span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd>Reviews state that roadside parking is available with limited space, but this is not verified by official sources <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://travel.trueid.net/detail/BmRGGWx9g1P7" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://www.wongnai.com/attractions/583288JQ-%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A5%E0%B9%87%E0%B8%81-%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%8D%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B9%E0%B8%87" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://travel.trueid.net/detail/BmRGGWx9g1P7" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Contact information ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>From a tin dredger to a workers' bridge</h3><p class="era-years">1960-1968 CE (2503-2511 BE)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The bridge's story began in Takua Pa during the tin-mining era, when the Boonsung dredging company stood on the opposite bank from the old market. The Takua Pa canal was more than 40 metres wide, so workers and residents had to row across, especially when floodwaters rose. The local database of Prince of Songkla University states that mining operator Juti Boonsung therefore first initiated a wooden bridge for walking and cycling</p><p>Later, in 1968 CE (2511 BE), steel from a decommissioned dredger was assembled into Khok Khanuen Iron Bridge, more than 200 metres long, across the Takua Pa River. The bridge was therefore not only industrial infrastructure, but also a shortcut for workers, a goods route, and a daily connection between the old market and the town's tin-driven mining area. Verifiable evidence confirms the mining and transport roles, but no contemporary document has been found directly linking this bridge to details about maritime trade, Hokkien Chinese people, or the town-governor system</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://clib.psu.ac.th/southerninfo/content/1/de645890" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ฐานข้อมูลท้องถิ่นภาคใต้ มหาวิทยาลัยสงขลานครินทร์ (Southern Thai Local Database, Prince of Songkla University)</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4421" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>When the mines went quiet, the bridge became a mining town trace</h3><p class="era-years">After 1968 CE (2511 BE) and before 2026 CE (2569 BE)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>When mining ended, the bridge did not disappear with the dredging plant. It changed from a work structure into a community route and evidence of the industrial landscape. ONEP sources state that the old dredging plant, preserved in its original condition, can still be seen from the bridge area, while contemporary tourism sources call the bridge a symbol of Takua Pa's mining-town past</p><p>Later, the bridge was described and presented as a tourist and photography spot, and it also appeared as a location in the film Wonderful Town (2007), according to an article tracking filming locations. However, this review found no evidence confirming when the mine closed, when major repairs took place, any direct impact from the 2004 tsunami, or registration as a historic site by the Fine Arts Department. These events should therefore not be added as facts</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4421" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</a> · <a href="https://th.readme.me/p/40233" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wonderful Town filming locations</a> · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/travel" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Tourist attractions</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A mining heritage that remains a passageway and destination</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Today, Boonsung Iron Bridge still serves as a community route. Field information and reviews say that residents use it for travel and motorcycles pass through. At the same time, Takua Pa Municipality classifies it as a tourist attraction, and a TAT tourism source has current images of the site. The bridge thus stands between functioning infrastructure and a landmark for walking, views, and photography</p><p>The latest evidence found is an NBT report dated 30 January 2026, which introduces the bridge as mining heritage associated with Takua Pa and says it was temporarily closed at that time to accommodate a foreign film shoot. In addition, a municipal budget document found includes items for maintaining and improving the bridge entrance area, but no document has been found confirming a restoration project for the structure itself. Opening and closing hours, admission fees, an activity-specific custodian, and the latest safety condition therefore still need to be checked on site</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/travel" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Tourist attractions</a> · <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QUZ54DTc0LQ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NBT2HD, Morning News, 30 January 2026</a> · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_form/2020-07_bc4d766e789d542.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบัญญัติงบประมาณเทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality Budget Ordinance)</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1960 CE (2503 BE)</p><h3>Juti Boon Soong took over the mining business</h3><p>Local databases indicate that Mr. Juti Boon Soong bought the Takua Pa Valley dredging company and discovered commuting difficulties for workers and locals between the old market and the company area.</p><a href="https://clib.psu.ac.th/southerninfo/content/1/de645890" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1968 CE (2511 BE)</p><h3>Construction of Khok Khanoon iron bridge</h3><p>Iron from a decommissioned tin dredger was used to build a bridge over 200 metres long across the Takua Pa River, connecting the town with the mining area and factory.</p><a href="https://clib.psu.ac.th/southerninfo/content/1/de645890" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">2007 (2550)</p><h3>Featured as a location in the film Wonderful Town</h3><p>Articles tracking filming locations state that the bridge was a setting in the Thai film Wonderful Town. This is not verified by official production documents, only by audience articles.</p><a href="https://th.readme.me/p/40233" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2020 (2563 BE)</p><h3>Municipality included the bridge entrance area in budget documents</h3><p>Discovered municipal budget documents contain an item for the maintenance and improvement of land and structures around the entrance of the Boon Soong iron bridge. This is not evidence of a restoration of the bridge itself.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_form/2020-07_bc4d766e789d542.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">30 January 2026</p><h3>NBT reported the bridge as a mining heritage site</h3><p>NBT reported that the bridge is a historical landmark and was temporarily closed that week to accommodate the filming of a foreign movie.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QUZ54DTc0LQ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>The wooden bridge came first</h3><p>A wooden bridge was built for workers to walk and cycle across the canal, as well as for locals to transport goods, but the reviewed sources do not specify the exact year.</p><a href="https://clib.psu.ac.th/southerninfo/content/1/de645890" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Steel structure about 200 metres long</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The bridge spans the Takua Pa river and connects the main road area with the old ore dredger site.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4421" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Traces of the mining industry</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Built with steel from a decommissioned tin dredger, and the old dredger can be seen at the end of the bridge.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4421" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Fields and mountain views</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>From the bridge, green fields, trees, and mountain ranges are visible, making it suitable for sightseeing and photography.</p><a href="https://travel.trueid.net/detail/BmRGGWx9g1P7" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Community transit route</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The bridge is still a route used by villagers, so one should be careful of vehicles while visiting.</p><a href="https://clib.psu.ac.th/southerninfo/content/1/de645890" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2026-01-30 · NBT2HD</p><h3>Inviting check-ins at Boon Soong iron bridge, mining heritage of Takua Pa town</h3><p>NBT presented the bridge as a mining heritage site and historical landmark, noting its temporary closure for a foreign film production.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QUZ54DTc0LQ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The iron bridge structure was built using steel from a decommissioned tin dredger, not new steel produced specifically for the bridge.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4421" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Before the iron bridge, workers and villagers had to use rowboats to cross the canal, and there used to be a wooden bridge for walking and cycling.</p><a href="https://clib.psu.ac.th/southerninfo/content/1/de645890" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p>The bridge appeared in a location tracking article for the film Wonderful Town (2007).</p><a href="https://th.readme.me/p/40233" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Travel along Rat Bamrung Road towards Takua Pa old town; the bridge is on the left, about 2 kilometres from the town centre.</p><a href="https://travel.trueid.net/detail/BmRGGWx9g1P7" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li><a href="/en/places/governor-wall/">Governor’s Residence Wall</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/khun-in/">Khun In House</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/tao-ming/">Tao Ming School</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Opening hours</summary><p>Information not verified · Open to visitors all day (information from a secondary tourism source)</p></details><details><summary>Is parking available?</summary><p>Reviews state that roadside parking is available with limited space, but this is not verified by official sources</p></details><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Travel along Rat Bamrung Road towards Takua Pa old town; the bridge is on the left, about 2 kilometres from the town centre.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>In 1968 (B.E. 2511), steel from a mining dredger was used to build the Khok Khanun Iron Bridge, more than 200 metres long, across the Takua Pa River. The initiative came from Juti Boonsung, owner of Juti Boonsung Mining Dredger Co., Ltd., founded in 1960 (B.E. 2503).</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>The bridge crosses the Takua Pa River, linking the main road area with the former mining plant. It uses steel from a decommissioned mining dredger, and the old plant is still visible at the far end. From the bridge, you can see green fields, trees, and mountain ranges, making it suitable for views and photography.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning (ONEP): Iron Bridge (Khok Khanun)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4421" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ฐานข้อมูลท้องถิ่นภาคใต้ มหาวิทยาลัยสงขลานครินทร์ (Southern Thai Local Database, Prince of Songkla University)</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://clib.psu.ac.th/southerninfo/content/1/de645890" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">TrueID Travel: Boonsung Iron Bridge</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://travel.trueid.net/detail/BmRGGWx9g1P7" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">TAT Media Assets: Boon Soong Iron Bridge</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1098453" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Tourist attractions</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/travel" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wongnai: Boonsung Iron Bridge</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.wongnai.com/attractions/583288JQ-%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A5%E0%B9%87%E0%B8%81-%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%8D%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B9%E0%B8%87" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4421" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบัญญัติงบประมาณเทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality Budget Ordinance)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_form/2020-07_bc4d766e789d542.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">NBT2HD Morning News</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QUZ54DTc0LQ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">TAT Media Assets: Image file 1594919</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1594919" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">TAT Media Assets: Image file 1098453</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1098453" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wonderful Town filming locations</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://th.readme.me/p/40233" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Phone number, Facebook page, website, or official LINE of the location not found.</li><li>Admission fee from checked sources not found.</li><li>Official data regarding restrooms, parking, and wheelchair access not found.</li><li>Verified distance or route data from Phuket, Khao Lak, or the airport not found.</li><li>Festival data specific to the bridge not found.</li><li>Evidence verifying the year and designer of the wooden or iron bridge, aside from the 1968 data and Mr Chuti Boon Soong, not found.</li><li>Evidence of historical site registration by the Fine Arts Department not verified yet.</li><li>Evidence that the bridge features Sino-Portuguese or Chinese architecture not found, so it cannot be concluded as such.</li><li>Nearby places with a verified walking distance from read sources not found.</li><li>Evidence verifying the year the mine closed or changes in ownership after the dredging company era not found.</li><li>Evidence verifying the year and details of the bridge restoration not found.</li><li>Evidence confirming direct impact from the 2004 tsunami not found.</li><li>Registration as a historical site by the Fine Arts Department not found.</li><li>Name of the agency or person directly responsible for the bridge structure in 2026 not found.</li><li>Announcements for opening hours, admission fees, restrooms, parking, or latest safety standards not found.</li><li>Historical photos with a public URL and clear sources not found.</li><li>Photos from TAT have a file listing page, but usage rights are unknown and require permission before use.</li><li>News from the past 5 years confirming restoration projects, traditional events, or awards specific to the bridge not found.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
.\audit\a2-enq.log:230:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Where to Eat and Rest in Takua Pa · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="Restaurants, cafes and snack stops in Takua Pa that the guide author has visited, with real opening hours and map links, plus a printable walking leaflet."><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Where to Eat and Rest in Takua Pa"><meta property="og:description" content="Restaurants, cafes and snack stops in Takua Pa that the guide author has visited, with real opening hours and map links, plus a printable walking leaflet."><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/rest/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/default.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/default.png"><meta name="generator" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/rest/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Takua Pa food, cafés, and places to stop", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/rest/"}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/rest/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/rest/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/rest/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/" aria-current="page">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/rest/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="intro"><a class="eyebrow" href="/en/">Takua Pa 101 / Old Town Guide</a><h1>Take a break, eat and explore Takuapa</h1><p class="lead">Shops and stops personally visited by the people who made this guide, with opening hours and directions</p></div><p>The whole old town is walkable, but there is little shade and the afternoon sun is strong. Stops along the way make it easier to cover the area.</p><p class="small">The list below is selected from<a href="https://siwaracafe.com/guide" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Siwara Cafe's Takua Pa food and travel guide</a> The people who made this website · Unlike the list of shops on<a href="/en/eat/">the Food and Souvenirs page</a> Every shop listed here has been visited in person, so the opening hours and coordinates are practical and current · Even so, small shops can change their hours at any time, so call ahead before making a long trip.</p><h2>Restaurants and food</h2><div class="rest-stops"><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Baan%20Lapp%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-baan-lapp.webp" alt="BAAN LAPP บ้านลัพพ์ (โฮมมี่ &amp; สเต๊ก ตะกั่วป่า)" width="1200" height="1600" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>BAAN LAPP (Homey &amp; Steak, Takua Pa)</h3><p>A warm, homey restaurant and cafe with a Hidden Gem style, serving steak, pasta, and carefully prepared fusion dishes.</p><p class="pick-meta">Open 11:00 - 21:00 (closed Wednesdays) · ~2.2 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">From 17:30 onward, the lights create a pleasant atmosphere. It is suitable for a family dinner.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Baan%20Lapp%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B9%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B0%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%95%E0%B9%8A%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%84%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B9%E0%B9%81%E0%B8%AD%E0%B9%8B%E0%B8%A7" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-moo-satay-kruaew.webp" alt="ขนมจีนหมูสะเต๊ะครูแอ๋ว (ทุ่งพระโพธิ์)" width="1590" height="1600" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Kru Aew's Khanom Chin and Pork Satay (Thung Phra Pho)</h3><p>A tucked-away shop in Thung Phra Pho serving tender, juicy charcoal-grilled pork satay marinated with spices, hot off the grill with boldly flavored southern Thai khanom chin and curry.</p><p class="pick-meta">Open 12:00 - 18:00 (closed Thursdays) · ~2.4 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">The pork satay is grilled fresh, skewer by skewer. A large set of 20 to 30 skewers is recommended with the khanom chin.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B9%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B0%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%95%E0%B9%8A%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%84%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B9%E0%B9%81%E0%B8%AD%E0%B9%8B%E0%B8%A7" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B5%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%82%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%87" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-mee-talad-khwang.webp" alt="บะหมี่พังงา ตลาดขวาง" width="1024" height="683" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Phang Nga Noodles, Khwang Market</h3><p>Springy, tender handmade egg noodles made with an old Hokkien recipe, tossed with fragrant fried garlic oil and large pieces of crispy pork lard, for a balanced, mellow flavor.</p><p class="pick-meta">Open 09:00 - 15:30 (closed Tuesdays) · ~0.6 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">Try the "special dry tom yum noodles with crispy pork lard". Toss well and enjoy without adding seasoning.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B5%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%82%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%87" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B5%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%AE%E0%B8%81%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B5%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%99" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-pa-da-hokkien.webp" alt="ป้าดา หมี่ฮกเกี้ยน (ถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า)" width="1600" height="1600" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Pa Da Hokkien Noodles (Thanon Si Takua Pa)</h3><p>A long-running Hokkien noodle shop on Thanon Si Takua Pa. The springy noodles are stir-fried with a fragrant wok-charred aroma, plenty of seafood, and a runny egg.</p><p class="pick-meta">Open 07:00 - 17:00 (daily) · ~0.7 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">Try the "Hokkien noodles stir-fried with a runny egg". Break the yolk and mix it into the hot noodles for a rich, savory taste.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B5%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%AE%E0%B8%81%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B5%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%99" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%B5%E0%B8%99%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-bang-deen.webp" alt="ร้านบังดีน ข้าวหมกไก่ &amp; โรตีแกง (Michelin Guide)" width="1200" height="1600" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Bangdeen Chicken Biryani &amp; Curry Roti (Michelin Guide)</h3><p>A well-known Muslim breakfast restaurant recognized by the Michelin Guide. Fragrant, tender spiced chicken biryani is served with a bold dipping sauce, along with soft roti and chicken massaman curry.</p><p class="pick-meta">Open 06:00 - 13:30 (daily) · ~2.8 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">The roti dough is freshly kneaded and fried until crisp yet soft. Try the massaman curry roti with hot pulled tea.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%B5%E0%B8%99%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9B%E0%B8%B9%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%B3%20%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B5" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-pu-dam.webp" alt="ร้านปูดำ (บางนายสี)" width="1010" height="761" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Black Crab Restaurant (Bang Nai Si)</h3><p>A tucked-away restaurant beside a mangrove canal in Bang Nai Si, serving fresh wild black crab with firm, intensely sweet meat and boldly seasoned local-style dishes.</p><p class="pick-meta">Open 10:00 - 21:00 (daily) · ~3.2 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">Steamed black crab and crab fried rice are the most frequently ordered dishes. Call ahead to check fresh supplies or go before evening.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9B%E0%B8%B9%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%B3%20%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B5" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%81%E0%B9%8B%E0%B8%9C%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B9%84%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-kae-padthai.webp" alt="เก๋ ผัดไทย (ตลาดเก่าตะกั่วป่า)" width="1131" height="1600" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Kae Pad Thai (Takua Pa Old Market)</h3><p>A popular Pad Thai shop in the old town area. Chewy noodles stir-fried in a rich traditional tamarind sauce, with large, fresh, and bouncy shrimp.</p><p class="pick-meta">Open 16:30 to 21:30 (daily) · ~0.6 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">Fresh shrimp Pad Thai wrapped in egg is the specialty. Squeeze fresh lime over it and eat with banana blossom and pennywort. Flavorful without extra seasoning.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%81%E0%B9%8B%E0%B8%9C%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B9%84%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%88%E0%B9%8A%E0%B8%AD%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%20%E0%B8%9A%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B3%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%84%E0%B9%87%E0%B8%A1" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-jae-ouan.webp" alt="เจ๊อ้วน ทะเลสด (บ้านน้ำเค็ม)" width="1200" height="1600" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Jae Uan Talay Sod (Baan Nam Kem)</h3><p>A renowned seafood restaurant in the Baan Nam Kem area. Fresh ingredients delivered directly from fishing boats daily. Spicy seafood dip made with real lime. Evening seaside atmosphere.</p><p class="pick-meta">Hours: 10:30 to 21:30 (Daily) · ~11.5 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">Great for dinner. Large tiger prawns with firm, sweet meat paired with spicy seafood dip.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%88%E0%B9%8A%E0%B8%AD%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%20%E0%B8%9A%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B3%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%84%E0%B9%87%E0%B8%A1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article></div><h2>Stops and Attractions</h2><div class="rest-stops"><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%96%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%A8%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B5%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-old-town-street.webp" alt="ถนนวัฒนธรรมศรีตะกั่วป่า &amp; สตรีทอาร์ตตึกโบราณ" width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Thanon Si Takua Pa &amp; Old Building Street Art</h3><p>An old shophouse district with arched walkways (Five-Foot Way) featuring street art that tells the stories of the Baba people and the town's tin mining history.</p><p class="pick-meta">Hours: Open all day (09:00 to 17:00 recommended) · ~0.7 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">You can easily walk through various alleys connecting to Tao Sor pastry shops and old town eateries.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%96%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%A8%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B5%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B3%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B3%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-tam-nang.webp" alt="น้ำตกตำหนัง (อุทยานแห่งชาติศรีพังงา)" width="1600" height="1060" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Tam Nang Waterfall (Si Phang Nga National Park)</h3><p>A large waterfall in the middle of a lush rainforest in Si Phang-nga National Park. The water cascades down a 63-meter high cliff into a clear pool where Mahseer barbs swim.</p><p class="pick-meta">Hours: 08:30 to 16:30 (Daily) · ~21.8 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">Between 10:00 and 14:00, the sunlight hits the water surface beautifully. There is a shaded resting spot under large trees.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B3%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B3%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A5%E0%B9%87%E0%B8%81%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-iron-bridge.webp" alt="สะพานเหล็กบุญสูง (สะพานโคกขนุน)" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Boonsung Iron Bridge (Khok Khanun Bridge)</h3><p>A historical landmark from the prosperous tin mining era. Built from the steel parts of an old tin dredger, elegantly spanning the Takua Pa River.</p><p class="pick-meta">Hours: Open 24 hours (16:30 to 18:30 recommended) · ~2.3 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">Between 17:00 and 18:30, the sunset light shines through the steel bridge structure, turning it into a beautiful orange. Great for taking photos.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A5%E0%B9%87%E0%B8%81%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%94%E0%B9%83%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%8D%E0%B9%88%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-lad-yai.webp" alt="หลาดใหญ่ ถนนคนเดินสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่า" width="1600" height="1066" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Lad Yai, the old town cultural walking street</h3><p>A classic historical walking street. Thanon Si Takua Pa is closed to traffic so locals can set up stalls selling traditional food, local snacks, and crafts under Sino-Portuguese style lighting.</p><p class="pick-meta">Hours: Sundays only 15:30 to 20:30 · ~0.7 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">Open only on Sundays. Arriving around 17:00 is recommended when the orange sunlight beautifully lights up the classic old buildings for photos.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%94%E0%B9%83%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%8D%E0%B9%88%20%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article></div><h2>Souvenirs</h2><div class="rest-stops"><article class="rest-stop pick"><a class="pick-art" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%95%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%AA%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/guide/guide-tuangrat-taosor.webp" alt="เต้าส้อตวงรัตน์ (ต้นตำรับ 100 ปี)" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy"></a><div class="pick-body"><h3>Tao Sor Tuang Rat (100-year-old original recipe)</h3><p>A top souvenir of Takua Pa. Thin crispy crust with dense mung bean filling, scented with traditional candle smoke. The recipe has been passed down through generations.</p><p class="pick-meta">Hours: 08:00 to 17:00 (Daily) · ~0.6 km from Siwara</p><p class="pick-tip">The salted egg yolk filling is their signature. Best bought fresh out of the oven. Can be kept for 7 to 10 days.</p><a class="shop-nav" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%95%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%AA%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate ↗</a></div></article></div><h2>Walking Pamphlet</h2><div class="leaflet-block"><a class="leaflet-art" href="/assets/leaflet/takuapa-walk-leaflet.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/leaflet/leaflet-page-1.webp" alt="แผ่นพับเดินเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า หน้าแรก" width="1400" height="990" loading="lazy"></a><div class="leaflet-copy"><p>A two-page pamphlet detailing the wooden house and four stops on the route above. Print on A4 paper, fold in half, and carry it with you. No need to look at your phone in the sun.</p><div class="leaflet-actions"><a class="button" href="/assets/leaflet/takuapa-walk-leaflet.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">โหลดแผ่นพับ PDF · 7.6 MB</a><a class="text-link" href="/en/leaflet/">Read on the website instead ↗</a></div><p class="small">Created by<a href="https://siwaracafe.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Siwara Cafe</a> Creators of this guide · Free to distribute and print</p></div></div>
.\audit\a2-enq.log:234:7:    <h2>Short Walking Route from the Wooden House</h2><div class="short-walk"><article class="walk-point"><a href="/en/places/khun-in/"><img src="/assets/khun-in.webp" alt="บ้านขุนอินทร์" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"></a><div><h3><a href="/en/places/khun-in/">Khun In House</a></h3><p>Notice: Porch Roof and Openings</p><button data-trip-add="khun-in">Add to trip</button></div></article><article class="walk-point"><a href="/en/places/tao-ming/"><img src="/assets/tao-ming.webp" alt="โรงเรียนเต้าหมิง" width="1000" height="667" loading="lazy"></a><div><h3><a href="/en/places/tao-ming/">Tao Ming School</a></h3><p>Notice: Gable and Yellow Balcony</p><button data-trip-add="tao-ming">Add to trip</button></div></article><article class="walk-point"><a href="/en/places/guan-yu/"><img src="/assets/guan-yu.webp" alt="ศาลเจ้าพ่อกวนอู ซิ่นไช่ตึ๋ง" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"></a><div><h3><a href="/en/places/guan-yu/">Guan Yu / Sin Chai Tung Shrine</a></h3><p>Notice: Door and Red Details</p><button data-trip-add="guan-yu">Add to trip</button></div></article><article class="walk-point"><a href="/en/places/iron-bridge/"><img src="/assets/iron-bridge.webp" alt="สะพานเหล็กบุญสูง" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"></a><div><h3><a href="/en/places/iron-bridge/">Boon Soong Iron Bridge</a></h3><p>Notice: Steel Structure and Riverside Landscape</p><button data-trip-add="iron-bridge">Add to trip</button></div></article></div><p>Plan further: <a href="/en/trip/">Plan your trip ↗</a> · <a href="/en/map/">View town map ↗</a></p><aside class="source"><h2>Data Sources</h2><p>Compiled from<a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takua Pa Town Municipality brochure</a> · Data extracted September 6, 2026 (2569 BE). The document does not specify a publication date. Opening hours, shop status, and current schedules are not verified. Please check with the venue before traveling.</p></aside><s