.\audit\a2-enq.log:742:Takua Pa Town Municipality brochure
.\audit\a2-enq.log:874:The condition verified from official sources is that the building remains and has architectural value in applied Sino-Portuguese style. As for opening hours, admission fees, regular caretakers, interior access, wheelchair accessibility, and the 2026 (2569 BE) restoration project, there is still no verifiable public information. Therefore, one should contact the caretaker or municipality before traveling.
.\audit\a2-enq.log:1156:The latest evidence found is an NBT report dated 30 January 2026, which introduces the bridge as mining heritage associated with Takua Pa and says it was temporarily closed at that time to accommodate a foreign film shoot. In addition, a municipal budget document found includes items for maintaining and improving the bridge entrance area, but no document has been found confirming a restoration project for the structure itself. Opening and closing hours, admission fees, an activity-specific custodian, and the latest safety condition therefore still need to be checked on site
.\audit\a2-enq.log:1180:Discovered municipal budget documents contain an item for the maintenance and improvement of land and structures around the entrance of the Boon Soong iron bridge. This is not evidence of a restoration of the bridge itself.
